WEBVTT

03:07.270 --> 03:08.600
Good morning.

03:08.600 --> 03:11.350
Well, well,
look who's finally up.

03:11.350 --> 03:14.520
All right, everybody.
Here we go.

03:14.520 --> 03:16.230
Little circles with your knees.

03:16.230 --> 03:18.280
So nice of you to join us,
Natsuki.

03:18.280 --> 03:19.530
Remember to breathe.

03:19.530 --> 03:21.240
You could've woken me up,
you know.

03:21.240 --> 03:24.570
I'm sorry. I thought you said
you didn't need me to.

03:24.570 --> 03:27.040
...with your hands at your sides
for leg raises.

03:27.040 --> 03:29.620
Now get ready for part 2,

03:29.620 --> 03:32.790
where we raise our arms
high in the air.

03:32.790 --> 03:35.090
You're missing the exercises.

03:35.090 --> 03:37.300
...3, 4.

03:37.300 --> 03:40.300
Make sure you make big circles
with your arms.

03:40.300 --> 03:42.800
Good morning, Amane.

03:42.800 --> 03:44.390
I beat you today.

03:44.390 --> 03:46.260
On what?

03:46.260 --> 03:49.850
You said we would race to see
who got up earlier.

03:51.350 --> 03:54.860
All right, girls.
Focus on the exercises.

03:54.860 --> 03:56.690
You forgot, didn't you?

03:56.690 --> 03:58.070
I didn't forget.

03:59.190 --> 04:01.070
I just didn't remember,
that's all.

04:01.070 --> 04:03.280
Same difference.

04:04.240 --> 04:06.370
I'm really sorry, OK?

04:16.840 --> 04:19.000
Morning, Tama. You good?

04:22.300 --> 04:25.510
Mom, my alarm broke, see?

04:25.510 --> 04:28.260
So could you buy me
a new one, please?

04:28.260 --> 04:30.680
Have you tried fixing it first?

04:31.930 --> 04:33.690
Fix it?

04:37.860 --> 04:41.190
Will you put that thing away?
We're eating now.

04:41.190 --> 04:44.360
It's a shame when a man
can't enjoy a simple breakfast

04:44.360 --> 04:46.410
with his family.

04:46.410 --> 04:48.490
Sorry. Force of habit.

04:51.580 --> 04:54.370
How were things
in the field today?

04:54.370 --> 04:56.960
It happened again.
Someone poached the crops.

04:56.960 --> 04:59.090
Maybe you should report it
to the police.

05:00.420 --> 05:03.010
They're no help.
I'll just catch them myself.

05:03.010 --> 05:05.840
Grandpa's wasabi
is just too irresistible.

05:08.350 --> 05:09.600
Fear not.

05:09.600 --> 05:10.890
When things go wrong,

05:10.890 --> 05:12.810
Miss Summer Vacation
will come to the rescue.

05:12.810 --> 05:14.640
Who's that?

05:14.640 --> 05:17.400
Why, it's my alter ego,
of course,

05:17.400 --> 05:20.110
a mysteriously cool superhero.

05:20.110 --> 05:21.940
Wasn't she called
Miss Summer Lady last year?

05:21.940 --> 05:23.570
- Bon appetit.
- Bon appetit.

05:23.570 --> 05:25.700
She must have transformed again.

05:25.700 --> 05:28.620
So is she still a superhero?

05:28.620 --> 05:30.740
So good.

05:30.740 --> 05:33.540
Welcome to the first game of
the Summer Baseball Championship

05:33.540 --> 05:35.040
at Koshien.

05:39.580 --> 05:41.170
Do you have everything?

05:42.550 --> 05:43.960
Here.

05:45.170 --> 05:46.630
Thank you.

05:55.600 --> 05:57.060
No!

05:57.060 --> 05:59.310
Stop it,
or you're going to be late.

05:59.310 --> 06:01.360
Natsuki, she's all yours.

06:01.360 --> 06:03.280
Aye, aye, captain.

06:03.280 --> 06:06.070
Hold on tight.
It's gonna be fast.

06:06.070 --> 06:07.780
I said, hold on tight.

06:07.780 --> 06:09.870
I'll be fine.

06:14.040 --> 06:16.750
Here we go!

06:16.750 --> 06:18.670
- Be careful.
- Bye.

06:41.730 --> 06:45.230
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

06:45.230 --> 06:48.150
I'll have your lunch packed
real soon, OK, honey?

06:48.150 --> 06:49.450
It's all right.

06:49.450 --> 06:50.950
You just got
off the night shift.

06:50.950 --> 06:52.990
You'll be gone
for an entire week.

06:52.990 --> 06:55.830
This is the least
I can do for you.

06:55.830 --> 06:59.250
Well, them let me help.
I can make the rice balls.

06:59.250 --> 07:02.250
It's amazing
how tall you're getting.

07:02.250 --> 07:04.540
I don't feel taller.

07:04.540 --> 07:06.840
Bye! See you later!

07:06.840 --> 07:09.970
- See you later.
- Good-bye.

07:09.970 --> 07:11.840
OK. Good luck out there.

07:11.840 --> 07:13.720
Bye-bye.

07:25.860 --> 07:29.190
COSMOS STORE

07:30.280 --> 07:33.160
Koji, what are you
bringing those for?

07:33.160 --> 07:35.740
I'm gonna read them
to my friends.

07:38.120 --> 07:40.410
It gets boring there sometimes.

07:40.410 --> 07:42.580
Do you want to take
my PlayStation, then?

07:42.580 --> 07:44.170
I don't want to be the loner

07:44.170 --> 07:46.670
who's playing video games
the entire time.

07:46.670 --> 07:49.340
When I was your age, we used
to go camping down by the river.

07:49.340 --> 07:51.800
They're far too young to be
camping out by the river,

07:51.800 --> 07:53.890
and there are only 4 of them
in the whole school.

07:53.890 --> 07:57.810
5. Amane's cousin Natsuki
just transferred.

07:57.810 --> 07:59.890
Oh, yeah? What's she like?

08:01.140 --> 08:02.770
She's kind of spacey.

08:02.770 --> 08:05.360
She's the one who let
Pyon-Kichi escape.

08:08.900 --> 08:12.650
Mommy said she's glad
you're leaving.

08:12.650 --> 08:15.620
Here you go, Noriko.
It's freshly squeezed.

08:15.620 --> 08:17.870
Hiroto, how many times
do I have to tell you

08:17.870 --> 08:19.790
to put on some pants
when you're outside?

08:19.790 --> 08:21.660
But I'm still inside the gate.

08:23.370 --> 08:25.630
OK. I'm going now.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.590
I can come up later
if you need anything.

08:27.590 --> 08:29.050
I'll be fine.

08:29.050 --> 08:31.010
I'll just send you an e-mail
if I need something.

08:31.010 --> 08:33.090
Besides, Kiyoshi'll
look after us.

08:44.140 --> 08:46.100
Do you need these tents?

08:46.100 --> 08:47.560
No, thanks.

08:47.560 --> 08:48.980
We're just gonna sleep
in the classroom.

08:48.980 --> 08:50.360
Got it.

08:56.860 --> 09:01.830
- Good morning.

08:56.870 --> 08:59.200
- Good morning.

08:59.200 --> 09:01.830
- Morning.

09:01.830 --> 09:04.410
- You're late.
- What?

09:04.410 --> 09:06.370
We're really the last ones?

09:07.040 --> 09:08.840
Afraid so.

09:08.840 --> 09:10.710
I hate being last.

09:10.710 --> 09:12.710
It's not a race, you know.

09:12.710 --> 09:14.510
I know, but still--

09:14.510 --> 09:16.970
Noriko, could you put this
in the fridge for me?

09:16.970 --> 09:18.680
Sure. No problem.

09:22.270 --> 09:28.110
PYON-KICHI'S HOUSE

09:31.860 --> 09:33.570
He hasn't come back?

09:34.860 --> 09:36.780
Still gone.

09:47.670 --> 09:50.130
You still mad at me
about Pyon-Kichi?

09:51.420 --> 09:53.800
I'm not mad. I'm just--

09:53.800 --> 09:56.010
I really didn't think
he'd run away.

09:57.430 --> 09:58.720
Don't feel bad.

09:58.720 --> 10:01.260
I'll buy you
a brand-new bunny, OK?

10:01.260 --> 10:02.760
No, thank you.

10:02.760 --> 10:05.350
- Well, what--
- You're not helping!

10:05.350 --> 10:06.730
What--

10:11.480 --> 10:13.110
All right.

10:13.110 --> 10:15.610
So I guess I'll be back
in a week at around 6:00.

10:15.610 --> 10:18.410
OK. I really appreciate
all your help.

10:18.410 --> 10:20.030
Good luck this year.

10:20.030 --> 10:22.120
- Thank you.
- Don't come and check on us.

10:22.120 --> 10:24.330
Right.

10:24.330 --> 10:27.290
When have we ever come up
to check on you?

10:27.290 --> 10:30.790
Besides, you're in good hands
with Kiyoshi.

10:41.220 --> 10:43.640
SUMMER CAMP

10:43.640 --> 10:46.390
LOOK AFTER YOURSELF.

10:43.640 --> 10:46.390
ONE FOR ALL, ALL FOR ONE.

10:50.600 --> 10:52.440
So what do we do now?

10:52.440 --> 10:55.860
I want someone to play this game
on my cell with me.

10:55.860 --> 10:57.150
Maybe later.

10:57.150 --> 10:59.860
We still have
plenty of homework to do.

11:10.290 --> 11:14.090
On second thought,
it is just the first day.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.170
Why don't we go look
for Pyon-Kichi?

11:16.170 --> 11:18.090
Really?

11:18.090 --> 11:21.300
I'll bet he misses us
and is super homesick by now.

11:22.760 --> 11:25.010
Pyon-Kichi?

11:26.770 --> 11:28.390
Pyon-Kichi?

11:32.230 --> 11:34.270
Pyon-Kichi?

11:34.270 --> 11:36.110
Slow down, Amane.

11:36.110 --> 11:38.360
You guys need to speed up.

11:38.360 --> 11:46.370
Pyon-Kichi?

11:47.490 --> 11:49.910
Come on. Help us look.

11:49.910 --> 11:52.250
I am looking.

11:57.170 --> 12:01.220
Do you know why Pyon-Kichi
ran away in the first place?

12:01.220 --> 12:03.590
I mean, he was
a pretty mellow bunny.

12:06.350 --> 12:09.470
It happened right here
on the last day of school.

12:13.350 --> 12:15.810
Look at all the trees
and the fresh air.

12:15.810 --> 12:17.440
Isn't it great?

12:17.440 --> 12:19.730
I'm gonna set you down
so you can play a bit.

12:19.730 --> 12:21.440
I'm gonna teach you
how to shake hands,

12:21.440 --> 12:24.280
and eventually,
I'm gonna teach you a backflip.

12:24.280 --> 12:28.490
Amane is gonna be so impressed.
It'll be fun.

12:33.960 --> 12:35.710
What were you thinking?

12:35.710 --> 12:38.170
Every superhero
needs a sidekick,

12:38.170 --> 12:41.380
and I was kind of hoping
he'd be mine.

12:42.630 --> 12:45.050
You're an idiot,
you know that?

12:45.050 --> 12:48.890
Oh, man, I hope
we find him soon.

12:50.640 --> 12:52.310
You thirsty?

13:08.950 --> 13:11.540
Koji, what happened?

13:11.540 --> 13:13.790
I fell.

13:13.790 --> 13:15.580
Are you OK?

13:15.580 --> 13:18.380
I'm fine.

13:18.380 --> 13:21.630
Stay where you are.
We'll be right there, OK?

13:38.100 --> 13:39.440
They're called crop circles.

13:39.440 --> 13:41.150
Some people think
they're made by UFOs.

13:41.150 --> 13:42.780
It's one of the world's
great mysteries.

13:42.780 --> 13:44.780
- UFOs?
- Neato.

13:45.900 --> 13:48.070
I thought these things
were just a hoax.

13:48.070 --> 13:51.030
At least, that's
what they said on TV.

13:51.030 --> 13:54.870
Yeah, but who would play such
a trick on our tiny village?

13:54.870 --> 13:57.000
- Hiroto would.
- Yeah, right.

13:57.000 --> 13:58.960
My brother would never be able
to pull this off.

13:58.960 --> 14:01.500
- A locust.
- Where?

14:01.500 --> 14:04.760
Maybe someone just spilled
some pesticide or something.

14:04.760 --> 14:09.010
Take a picture of it, Noriko.
I want to put it on our website.

14:09.010 --> 14:10.760
OK. Sure.

14:10.760 --> 14:12.470
- Make sure it's good.
- Gotcha.

14:12.470 --> 14:14.140
This is
a life-changing discovery.

14:14.140 --> 14:16.480
Oh, great, no pressure
or anything.

14:16.480 --> 14:18.900
You know I don't do well
under pressure.

14:27.740 --> 14:29.780
Pyon-Kichi.

14:30.570 --> 14:32.030
Pyon-Kichi?

14:34.410 --> 14:36.450
Pyon-Kichi?

14:38.000 --> 14:40.540
Not him.

14:46.260 --> 14:48.050
Are you OK?

14:55.430 --> 14:58.180
- Is that a dog?
- What do we do?

14:58.180 --> 15:00.060
He looks hurt.

15:00.060 --> 15:01.940
Noriko, give me
your handkerchief.

15:12.570 --> 15:14.530
Hit it hard, Koji!

15:14.530 --> 15:16.490
You can do it, Kiyoshi.

15:24.210 --> 15:26.210
- Get him!
- Run! Run!

15:26.210 --> 15:27.590
Go get him!

15:29.050 --> 15:31.050
Throw it at him.

15:32.050 --> 15:34.850
- You're out.
- Nice try!

15:36.180 --> 15:38.810
- One more out left.
- Oh, man, I almost made it.

15:41.310 --> 15:43.770
You better go long, Kiyoshi.

15:45.190 --> 15:47.980
Don't listen to her.
Strike her out.

15:47.980 --> 15:50.400
Yeah. Strike her out.

15:52.950 --> 15:54.910
It's a home run.

16:09.010 --> 16:10.420
My home run.

16:10.420 --> 16:13.010
Look. He's all better now.

16:16.680 --> 16:19.180
That is one well-trained dog.

16:21.890 --> 16:24.770
There's something I must say.

16:24.770 --> 16:27.860
Thank you. You saved my life.

16:32.240 --> 16:34.320
My name is Pochi.

16:34.320 --> 16:37.740
I'm from Planet Wan Bow
in the Animal Stellar Region.

16:45.630 --> 16:48.540
I just can't stop thinking
of you as a dog.

16:50.170 --> 16:53.510
To be lumped in the same
category as those beasts.

16:54.300 --> 16:56.390
Here's proof--my I.D.

16:56.390 --> 16:58.470
So you really are an alien.

16:58.470 --> 17:00.430
Yep. Told you so.

17:02.980 --> 17:05.810
Was that written in alien?

17:05.810 --> 17:07.060
Yeah.

17:07.060 --> 17:08.770
How come you can speak
our language?

17:08.770 --> 17:10.650
Well, I studied it.

17:10.650 --> 17:14.530
Of course, I can only carry on
simple conversations.

17:19.330 --> 17:20.870
Looks like a dog's butt.

17:20.870 --> 17:23.580
Hey, watch it!
What do you think you're doing?

17:23.580 --> 17:26.040
That is just rude.
You got some nerve.

17:29.670 --> 17:32.840
So, Pochi,
what brings you to Earth?

17:35.300 --> 17:37.930
I've come here to study
your plants.

17:37.930 --> 17:39.430
- Study our plants?
- What?

17:39.430 --> 17:42.100
Well, I found a species
that's been extinct

17:42.100 --> 17:43.810
for 5 billion years.

17:43.810 --> 17:45.640
5 billion?

17:45.640 --> 17:47.560
I wonder what kind
of plant it is.

17:47.560 --> 17:49.900
I have no idea what it could be.

17:51.070 --> 17:53.230
The plant flowers
are called Zughaan,

17:53.230 --> 17:55.360
and they are beautiful,
like you.

17:56.820 --> 18:00.780
18 years ago, microparticles
believed to be from Zughaan

18:00.780 --> 18:02.620
showed up on the black market.

18:04.540 --> 18:07.920
I've searched all through space
for their origin.

18:07.920 --> 18:10.250
I finally found them
on your planet.

18:14.630 --> 18:17.050
It's been forbidden
to remove species

18:17.050 --> 18:18.800
from an undeveloped planet.

18:18.800 --> 18:20.720
So I stay here
to do my research,

18:20.720 --> 18:22.430
and that's when
the poachers came.

18:22.430 --> 18:23.890
I fought them
with everything I had,

18:23.890 --> 18:26.020
refusing to let them steal
what's not theirs,

18:26.020 --> 18:27.980
but I got injured
in the battle, and--

18:32.110 --> 18:33.730
Are you OK?

18:33.730 --> 18:35.150
Of course.

18:37.860 --> 18:41.120
I'm fully recovered now,
and it's all thanks to you.

18:47.660 --> 18:50.080
I'm glad.

18:50.080 --> 18:52.210
What a scoop.

18:52.210 --> 18:54.050
It's like we're in the middle
of the movie

18:54.050 --> 18:56.550
"Close Encounters
of the Third Kind,"

18:56.550 --> 18:58.550
but it's not science fiction.

18:58.550 --> 18:59.800
Yeah.

18:59.800 --> 19:01.590
Hey, Pochi, can I write
a piece on this?

19:01.590 --> 19:05.180
Out of the question.
Intergalactic rules forbid it.

19:05.180 --> 19:07.390
That sucks.

19:10.100 --> 19:12.520
She's up.

19:14.070 --> 19:16.150
Oh, hey, I must have
scared you pretty bad.

19:16.150 --> 19:17.570
Sorry.

19:22.820 --> 19:24.030
Over here.

19:24.030 --> 19:26.080
- Hey, I'm gonna get you.
- Be careful.

19:43.930 --> 19:46.350
So do you think you scared
the poachers off for good?

19:46.350 --> 19:47.810
I can be very convincing.

19:47.810 --> 19:49.810
Besides, I'll increase
surveillance on your world

19:49.810 --> 19:51.730
once I get home.

19:51.730 --> 19:54.110
How long till you come back?

19:55.940 --> 19:58.650
I probably won't be coming back.

19:58.650 --> 20:00.740
- What?
- What?

20:00.740 --> 20:02.860
But we only just met you.

20:02.860 --> 20:05.240
Well, technically,
we should never have met.

20:05.240 --> 20:08.700
I'm supposed to avoid contact
with the local species.

20:08.700 --> 20:12.710
I wanted to learn a lot more
about space.

20:12.710 --> 20:14.540
I really am sorry.

20:17.210 --> 20:19.380
I'd like to offer you something
to thank you

20:19.380 --> 20:21.130
for everything you've done.

20:22.720 --> 20:26.100
Is there anything I could
possibly do for you?

20:27.140 --> 20:29.600
I know. Pyon-Kichi.

20:30.890 --> 20:32.940
Help us find Pyon-Kichi.

20:32.940 --> 20:35.560
Who's that?
Is he a friend of yours?

20:35.560 --> 20:39.030
- Yep.
- Our pet, a rabbit.

20:39.030 --> 20:41.990
His ear are so long, like this.

20:43.610 --> 20:46.160
I'm sorry, but I can't.

20:46.160 --> 20:47.740
What?

20:47.740 --> 20:51.830
Hey, that's OK.
We can do that on our own.

20:51.830 --> 20:53.830
Any other wishes?

20:56.460 --> 20:57.960
I know.

20:57.960 --> 21:00.500
Will you take me
on a school field trip, Kiyoshi?

21:01.380 --> 21:03.590
- What, me?
- That's right.

21:03.590 --> 21:05.930
They cancelled
the school trip this year.

21:05.930 --> 21:09.430
So I was hoping,
could you take us instead?

21:09.430 --> 21:12.480
Wouldn't be much fun to go there
with a teacher, I guess.

21:12.480 --> 21:14.810
I know. We should all go.

21:14.810 --> 21:17.360
Yes! Let's.

21:18.940 --> 21:21.440
Can we? Pretty please?

21:22.690 --> 21:25.320
- Sure.
- Where do you want to go?

21:25.320 --> 21:27.570
Well, how about
as far as possible?

21:27.570 --> 21:30.410
All right.
Your wish is my command.

21:30.410 --> 21:34.460
I'll take you to the moon, the
farthest mankind has traveled.

21:34.460 --> 21:36.540
- The moon?
- The moon?

21:42.300 --> 21:43.960
Oh, I can't look.

21:43.960 --> 21:46.800
On second thought, maybe we
should go someplace closer.

21:46.800 --> 21:50.220
It'll be OK.
You have nothing to worry about.

21:51.010 --> 21:52.390
Try to look at something.

21:52.390 --> 21:53.720
Hey, look.

22:22.380 --> 22:24.710
It's so blue.

22:24.710 --> 22:26.170
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

22:28.180 --> 22:30.300
The Hubble spacecraft.

22:34.390 --> 22:36.600
I want to tell
my friends about this,

22:36.600 --> 22:38.350
but who would ever believe me?

22:52.450 --> 22:54.830
Are we inside a UFO?

22:54.830 --> 22:56.540
From here, we take a taxi cab.

22:56.540 --> 22:58.460
- How come you're not floating?
- They have space taxis?

22:58.460 --> 23:01.040
It's high-techy
outer space stuff.

23:01.040 --> 23:02.920
Really?

23:07.380 --> 23:09.430
What did you say to that thing?

23:09.430 --> 23:11.340
I asked it to take us
to the moon.

23:21.270 --> 23:23.560
It's just like in the books.

23:23.560 --> 23:25.770
We actually made it to the moon.

23:25.770 --> 23:28.400
Kiyoshi! Look over here.

23:29.740 --> 23:32.320
- Take one of me, too.
- Yeah, me, too.

23:32.320 --> 23:35.280
Hey, Noriko,
take a picture of that.

23:37.830 --> 23:40.160
Careful. Don't get carried away.

23:40.160 --> 23:42.330
You haven't even seen
the real moon yet.

25:14.130 --> 25:16.430
The moon is incredible.

25:17.970 --> 25:19.720
We'll store your jungle gym here

25:19.720 --> 25:21.560
and pick it up
before we go home.

25:21.560 --> 25:22.890
OK.

25:26.850 --> 25:29.520
Look. I'm flying.

25:29.520 --> 25:33.360
- My legs are all wobbly.
- I got you. You're good.

25:39.330 --> 25:41.620
It's a robot.

25:41.620 --> 25:45.460
He's saying that you need
to go through immigration first.

25:45.460 --> 25:48.630
Don't worry about it.
You guys'll be fine. Let's go.

25:48.630 --> 25:50.540
Yeah.

26:02.140 --> 26:04.430
Your data will be stored
at the Space Control Center.

26:05.140 --> 26:06.520
What?

26:06.520 --> 26:08.650
Please declare your identity,
residence planet,

26:08.650 --> 26:10.610
and number of lifetime units.

26:10.610 --> 26:12.610
What?

26:12.610 --> 26:14.440
Please state your name.

26:14.440 --> 26:18.030
Suzuki Amane, and I'm 7.

26:19.450 --> 26:22.580
Welcome to the moon, Amane dear.

26:22.580 --> 26:24.200
Thank you?

26:24.200 --> 26:25.450
Your planet, the Earth,

26:25.450 --> 26:27.250
has not joined
the Space Federation yet--

26:27.250 --> 26:28.620
did you know that?--

26:29.420 --> 26:30.880
and because of that,

26:30.880 --> 26:32.750
you are not allowed
to travel in space...

26:32.750 --> 26:34.710
What? But that's bad, right?

26:34.710 --> 26:36.420
but if you pass this test,

26:36.420 --> 26:39.220
I can give you
a special visitor's passport.

26:39.220 --> 26:41.220
That's good.

26:41.220 --> 26:42.810
If you fail, though,
you'll be sent

26:42.810 --> 26:44.600
to the Lost Children's
Space Center...

26:44.600 --> 26:46.180
What?

26:46.180 --> 26:48.190
and you must stay there until
Earth joins the Federation.

26:48.190 --> 26:50.770
Here is the test.

26:50.770 --> 26:53.820
One day, a space alien
comes to visit you.

26:53.820 --> 26:55.400
He says that if you let him,

26:55.400 --> 26:57.400
he will make the people of Earth
very smart

26:57.400 --> 26:59.910
so there will be no more wars
and poor people

26:59.910 --> 27:03.450
and everyone will get along
and be happy.

27:03.450 --> 27:04.950
What do you think?

27:04.950 --> 27:07.580
Will you accept
the alien's offer?

27:18.550 --> 27:19.800
No.

27:19.800 --> 27:21.180
But why?

27:22.430 --> 27:25.060
It would be nice to be smart,

27:25.060 --> 27:28.930
and I want everyone
to be happy and all,

27:28.930 --> 27:33.690
but we should learn how to do
those things by ourselves.

27:33.690 --> 27:37.320
It's better that way.
That's what I learned in school.

27:37.320 --> 27:40.820
Everyone must
look after themselves.

27:47.290 --> 27:49.160
You passed.

27:49.160 --> 27:50.540
Really?

27:50.540 --> 27:52.920
Yes. You did a very good job.

27:56.550 --> 27:58.460
Yeah.

27:58.460 --> 28:00.590
- Amane.
- There you are.

28:00.590 --> 28:02.090
We were getting
a little worried.

28:02.090 --> 28:04.260
Yeah.

28:06.010 --> 28:08.560
Is that the passport you picked?

28:09.810 --> 28:11.270
This one is mine.

28:11.270 --> 28:13.190
I picked the same thing
as Kiyoshi.

28:13.190 --> 28:15.110
And I picked this.

28:15.110 --> 28:17.440
That's pretty.

28:18.480 --> 28:22.400
We still got to wait
for Natsuki.

28:26.330 --> 28:28.870
Don't worry. She'll pass.

28:28.870 --> 28:31.120
Why don't we try
putting your passport on?

28:31.120 --> 28:33.580
You're in for a surprise.

28:34.920 --> 28:40.420
Here. Let me help you,
and look up at those signs.

28:40.420 --> 28:42.310
WELCOME TO

28:40.420 --> 28:42.310
GREAT BEGINNER GATEWAY

28:43.760 --> 28:46.800
GALAXY SWEET BUNS

28:43.760 --> 28:46.800
SPACE BURGER

28:47.180 --> 28:49.810
RENTAL CRAFT FOR YOUR TRIP!

28:50.310 --> 28:53.770
NEW!

28:50.310 --> 28:53.770
TRY OUR GALAXY LOLLIPOPS!

28:53.770 --> 28:55.400
Ask the nearest
representative...

28:55.400 --> 28:57.060
I can read it now.

28:57.060 --> 28:59.480
We hope you enjoy
your stay with us.

29:00.980 --> 29:03.280
For those individuals
traveling...

29:03.280 --> 29:04.660
Try jumping.

29:04.660 --> 29:05.990
with a temporary passport...

29:05.990 --> 29:07.570
Yeah. Come on. Jump.

29:07.570 --> 29:09.030
familiarize yourselves...

29:09.030 --> 29:11.830
I'm not floating anymore.

29:11.830 --> 29:13.870
Isn't space technology great?

29:13.870 --> 29:15.540
...same codes of conduct

29:15.540 --> 29:18.750
as the citizens
of the Space Federation.

29:18.750 --> 29:22.510
Your cooperation is appreciated.

29:22.510 --> 29:25.470
Welcome to the moon,
and enjoy your stay.

29:25.470 --> 29:26.800
Yeah.

29:28.050 --> 29:30.220
Interesting.

29:32.470 --> 29:33.680
WELCOME TO

29:32.470 --> 29:33.680
GREAT BEGINNER GATEWAY

29:34.310 --> 29:34.980
ENJOY YOUR STAY

29:42.030 --> 29:43.940
Neato.

29:57.290 --> 29:59.290
- Did you see that?
- Yeah.

30:03.210 --> 30:05.340
Move it.
Watch where you're going.

30:06.880 --> 30:08.220
Sorry.

30:11.680 --> 30:14.640
There sure are a lot
of aliens here.

30:20.770 --> 30:22.980
Welcome to space, everyone.

30:28.570 --> 30:30.030
Treat are on me.

30:31.530 --> 30:33.740
- Space food.
- Yeah.

30:33.740 --> 30:37.540
I am so hungry,
I could eat a space cow.

30:37.540 --> 30:39.170
This food looks delicious.

30:40.460 --> 30:44.250
Welcome to Space Burger.
Are you ready to order?

30:45.380 --> 30:47.300
We'll take 6 Andro Burgers,

30:47.300 --> 30:49.840
all with Crystal Potatoes
and colas, please.

30:49.840 --> 30:52.390
Coming right up.

30:52.390 --> 30:55.470
Space Burger--
When You're Here, You're Family.

30:55.470 --> 30:58.060
They want two
Crystal Potatoes and a...

30:58.060 --> 31:01.100
This thing says a cola
costs one pod.

31:01.100 --> 31:03.400
So how many dollars is that?

31:03.400 --> 31:05.730
Who knows?

31:05.730 --> 31:07.900
Wait a sec.

31:07.900 --> 31:10.820
Pochi, how much
is a movie ticket?

31:10.820 --> 31:13.740
Well, for a kid's ticket,
it's only 6 pods.

31:13.740 --> 31:15.910
How much is it on Earth?

31:15.910 --> 31:18.000
It's about $11.

31:18.000 --> 31:20.120
Right. So that means
we divide 11 by 6

31:20.120 --> 31:22.290
to figure out
how many dollars one pod is.

31:22.290 --> 31:24.210
Makes sense.

31:24.210 --> 31:26.090
All right. Pop math quiz.

31:26.090 --> 31:27.630
- What?
- What?

31:27.630 --> 31:29.380
Come on. I'm timing you.

31:29.380 --> 31:32.010
I can't believe he's making us
do math right now.

31:33.930 --> 31:35.640
You don't have to do this,
Amane.

31:35.640 --> 31:39.390
Why not? I want to do it.

31:43.560 --> 31:45.110
Got it.

31:45.110 --> 31:48.110
The answer is 1.83333.

31:48.110 --> 31:51.030
So one pod is $1.83.

31:51.030 --> 31:52.820
Nicely done.

31:52.820 --> 31:55.120
- Really.
- Thank you for waiting.

31:57.580 --> 32:00.120
$1.83 for this?

32:00.710 --> 32:02.080
Expensive.

32:04.420 --> 32:06.340
It tastes just like on Earth.

32:06.340 --> 32:08.590
Cola is the same
everywhere, I guess.

32:10.380 --> 32:12.260
"The Space Show."

32:16.100 --> 32:19.640
"The Space Show"
is the bestest show ever.

33:01.270 --> 33:04.640
Hello, ladies and gentlealiens.

33:04.640 --> 33:07.230
May I present to you
the best space entertainment

33:07.230 --> 33:12.070
on any side of the galaxy--
"The Space Show"?

33:12.070 --> 33:14.360
Today we will be
broadcasting live

33:14.360 --> 33:17.490
from the Magellan
Antique Book Fair.

33:17.490 --> 33:22.200
My name is Neppo, and,
as always, I am your host.

33:22.200 --> 33:25.080
What's "The Space Show"?

33:25.080 --> 33:26.880
Hey, Pochi...

33:28.040 --> 33:30.710
I said, what's "The Space Show"?

33:30.710 --> 33:33.840
It's the most popular show
in space.

33:33.840 --> 33:35.840
What will he do?

33:35.840 --> 33:38.800
They have this stuff in space
just like us.

33:38.800 --> 33:41.310
It's a pirate show,
and it's broadcast live

33:41.310 --> 33:43.230
throughout every galaxy.

33:43.230 --> 33:45.390
You can broadcast
throughout all of space?

33:45.390 --> 33:46.690
That's right.

33:46.690 --> 33:49.020
Isn't there a time lag
or something?

33:49.020 --> 33:51.320
Well, it wouldn't be live
if there was.

33:51.320 --> 33:52.940
I guess that's true.

33:52.940 --> 33:54.610
Look.

33:54.610 --> 33:56.990
Look. Oh, pretty.

33:57.610 --> 33:59.950
What a pretty dog.

33:59.950 --> 34:01.540
She's not a dog.

34:01.540 --> 34:03.620
She comes
from the same planet I do.

34:03.620 --> 34:06.210
- What? No.
- Why is that so hard to believe?

34:06.210 --> 34:08.250
Then is she your friend?

34:09.460 --> 34:11.840
Sort of.

34:15.050 --> 34:17.430
What do you mean,
you came back empty-handed?

34:17.430 --> 34:19.510
Then what was the point
of going there?

34:19.510 --> 34:21.300
But law enforcement was there.

34:21.300 --> 34:23.890
We barely made it
back here alive.

34:23.890 --> 34:25.980
My whole life
flashed before my eyes, sir.

34:25.980 --> 34:27.980
I thought I was
a goner for sure.

34:27.980 --> 34:32.150
Yes, but on the bright side,
we have a souvenir for you.

34:32.150 --> 34:34.070
You are cowards, idiots.

34:34.070 --> 34:35.940
You will get me some Zughaan,

34:35.940 --> 34:38.740
even if it's the last thing
that you do.

34:38.740 --> 34:41.070
Ridiculous.

34:42.910 --> 34:45.330
The law, eh?

34:47.830 --> 34:49.790
I'm starving.

34:49.790 --> 34:52.420
Maybe we should go get
something to eat, then.

34:52.420 --> 34:54.250
Work first. Eat later.

34:54.250 --> 34:56.510
Shut up. You don't understand.

34:56.510 --> 35:00.260
A robot like you doesn't know
the pain of hunger.

35:00.260 --> 35:02.850
Oh, look. It's them.

35:02.850 --> 35:04.810
Fate brought
the two of them together.

35:04.810 --> 35:07.350
I thought "The Space Show"
was pretty interesting.

35:07.350 --> 35:08.770
Me, too.

35:08.770 --> 35:11.730
I want to be like Marie one day.
She's so pretty.

35:11.730 --> 35:14.520
You always want to be a star.

35:15.480 --> 35:17.530
I'd rather be the Iron Mask.

35:19.650 --> 35:21.450
Then I could be the hero.

35:21.450 --> 35:23.950
You can't be the hero.
You're a girl.

35:23.950 --> 35:26.580
So those are both
of your dreams, huh?

35:26.580 --> 35:29.500
And what about you, Miss Amane?
Do you have a dream?

35:30.170 --> 35:31.790
To be president.

35:31.790 --> 35:33.960
Good for you. Dream big.

35:33.960 --> 35:36.000
I want to be an astronomist.

35:37.460 --> 35:38.880
What about you, Kiyoshi?

35:40.510 --> 35:43.550
I don't care what I am,
as long as I can help others.

35:43.550 --> 35:45.510
So then you should be a doctor.

35:47.220 --> 35:48.890
We'll see.

35:48.890 --> 35:51.060
Your turn.

35:51.060 --> 35:53.980
Yeah. What did you want to be?

35:53.980 --> 35:55.690
I wanted to travel
all through space

35:55.690 --> 35:58.490
visiting different planets,
all in the name of research.

35:58.490 --> 36:00.740
It sounds like
your dream came true.

36:00.740 --> 36:02.530
You're lucky.

36:05.780 --> 36:07.740
I guess.

36:07.740 --> 36:09.160
I need to turn in my report

36:09.160 --> 36:12.170
and buy the tickets
for your flight back home.

36:12.170 --> 36:14.630
Why don't you all
go shopping while you wait?

36:15.460 --> 36:18.210
- Wow, 10 pods.
- We can't.

36:18.210 --> 36:20.800
Don't worry about it.
You saved my life.

36:20.800 --> 36:23.800
The least I can do is cover
your expenses on this trip.

36:25.050 --> 36:27.310
- OK.
- Yeah.

36:27.310 --> 36:29.390
Thank you, Pochi.

36:29.390 --> 36:31.060
Yeah. Thanks.

36:31.060 --> 36:32.310
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

36:32.310 --> 36:34.980
- Spend it wisely.
- We will.

36:34.980 --> 36:39.070
- I'm going to a toy store.
- Yeah. Toys.

36:45.200 --> 36:47.330
Not funny.

36:49.740 --> 36:51.410
That's cool.

36:51.410 --> 36:53.370
That's so gorge.

36:54.620 --> 36:55.880
Yeah.

36:55.880 --> 36:57.750
Wait for me.

36:57.750 --> 37:00.010
One, please.

37:07.430 --> 37:09.100
You see that?

37:09.100 --> 37:12.060
All of those
are aquatic aliens.

37:15.100 --> 37:17.020
To protect
this endangered vegetation,

37:17.020 --> 37:20.190
I strongly recommend enhanced
security of the geosphere.

37:20.190 --> 37:22.650
End report. Pochi Rickman.

37:22.650 --> 37:24.740
Submit identification.

37:26.280 --> 37:28.450
Verification complete.

37:38.290 --> 37:41.000
I have a coupon here
for a discount.

37:41.000 --> 37:42.920
Give me 3 tickets to Earth.

37:42.920 --> 37:45.380
- Impossible.
- Why's that?

37:45.380 --> 37:47.340
Because all of the routes
to Earth

37:47.340 --> 37:50.760
were recently suspended,
happened seconds ago.

37:50.760 --> 37:52.680
Tough luck, buddy.

37:55.890 --> 37:57.650
Say, "Space Show."

37:57.650 --> 38:00.360
- "Space Show."
- "Space Show."

38:00.360 --> 38:02.480
- Thank you very much.
- Bye.

38:02.480 --> 38:05.610
- Have a safe trip.
- Thank you.

38:13.500 --> 38:15.330
I have some bad news.

38:15.330 --> 38:16.620
What is it?

38:16.620 --> 38:18.420
They've blocked
all travel to Earth.

38:18.420 --> 38:20.500
- What?
- But why?

38:20.500 --> 38:25.340
Well, they took my report much
more seriously than I expected.

38:25.340 --> 38:27.970
It was because
of something you did?

38:27.970 --> 38:29.800
Stop it.

38:30.720 --> 38:33.720
This isn't Pochi's fault.

38:33.720 --> 38:36.100
No. Actually, it is his fault.

38:37.480 --> 38:40.360
So how long is this gonna last?

38:40.360 --> 38:42.230
No idea.

38:42.230 --> 38:43.980
Don't worry.
There's another way.

38:43.980 --> 38:47.070
We can get back to Earth if we
fly there from another planet.

38:47.070 --> 38:49.320
Another planet?

38:49.320 --> 38:52.450
That's right,
my home planet Wan Bow.

38:52.450 --> 38:54.040
Planet Wan Bow?

38:54.040 --> 38:56.160
- The planet of dogs?
- We're not dogs!

38:56.160 --> 38:58.620
How long till we get home?

38:59.870 --> 39:01.500
20 years or so.

39:01.500 --> 39:03.250
- 20 years?
- 20 years?

39:04.500 --> 39:06.550
Summer vacation will be over.

39:06.550 --> 39:08.880
Many summer vacations
will be over.

39:08.880 --> 39:11.680
I don't mean to be difficult,
but we're supposed to meet

39:11.680 --> 39:13.930
our parents at 6 P.M.
on the 7th.

39:13.930 --> 39:16.180
Is there any way
we can get back sooner?

39:16.180 --> 39:18.560
Well, if we took
the Galaxy Super Express,

39:18.560 --> 39:19.940
we could make it.

39:19.940 --> 39:21.100
We could?

39:21.100 --> 39:23.570
Yeah, but it's expensive,
though.

39:23.570 --> 39:25.780
Oh, money.

39:25.780 --> 39:28.280
Leave it to me.
I'll work it out.

39:36.120 --> 39:40.870
I will try to bring you
a souvenir.

39:40.870 --> 39:43.170
- Hope to see you soon.
- What are you doing?

39:43.170 --> 39:45.300
Sending Hiroto an email.

39:48.010 --> 39:50.260
You can still get service here?

39:51.550 --> 39:53.220
I still have some bars.

39:55.310 --> 39:58.350
Transmission is complete.

39:58.350 --> 40:00.480
She's sleeping like a log.

40:00.480 --> 40:03.020
It's already like 11 P.M.
back home.

40:14.780 --> 40:18.750
I'm very sorry.

40:19.660 --> 40:21.330
You mean about Pyon-Kichi?

40:25.500 --> 40:28.800
You should apologize
when she's awake.

40:28.800 --> 40:33.130
I did that, but she still
hasn't forgiven me.

40:33.130 --> 40:35.350
Besides, I'm older,
so it's weird for me

40:35.350 --> 40:37.890
to keep on apologizing to her.

40:43.690 --> 40:47.690
I can't believe everything
that's happened today.

40:57.700 --> 40:58.990
Bow wow?

40:58.990 --> 41:00.540
Dad, this is Pochi.

41:00.540 --> 41:01.750
Do you think I could borrow

41:01.750 --> 41:04.670
about 100,000 pods
from you right away?

41:05.830 --> 41:07.920
Oh, come on!

41:07.920 --> 41:09.840
Doesn't that sound like fun?

41:09.840 --> 41:12.470
1, 2, 3, 4...

41:12.470 --> 41:15.590
- 5, 6, 7, 8.
- 5, 6, 7, 8.

41:15.590 --> 41:18.470
1, 2, 3, 4...

41:18.470 --> 41:21.220
- 5, 6, 7, 8.
- 5, 6, 7, 8.

41:21.220 --> 41:24.140
1, 2, 3, 4...

41:24.140 --> 41:26.730
- 5, 6, 7, 8.
- 5, 6, 7, 8.

41:26.730 --> 41:31.030
So there's a slight issue.
My financial lender backed out.

41:32.530 --> 41:34.950
Where does that leave us?
Are we stranded here forever?

41:34.950 --> 41:37.410
Don't worry.
I'll raise the money somehow.

41:37.410 --> 41:40.290
I said I'd work it out,
didn't I?

41:40.290 --> 41:42.200
First, we got to find
a solid pick.

41:40.660 --> 41:42.700
RACE INFO

41:42.200 --> 41:43.910
Then we find
some more safe bets,

41:43.910 --> 41:46.210
and this last horse
will make or break us.

41:46.210 --> 41:48.590
Don't worry. I got this.

41:53.420 --> 41:55.550
I'll get a job.

41:55.550 --> 41:58.760
If I can earn money,
we can get home faster.

41:58.760 --> 42:00.720
I'll pick a place
to meet you afterwards.

42:00.720 --> 42:02.850
Stay there and wait for me.
Don't wander around.

42:02.850 --> 42:04.770
Then I'm gonna find a job, too.

42:05.600 --> 42:06.890
Me, too.

42:06.890 --> 42:08.350
- Yeah.
- Me, 4.

42:08.350 --> 42:12.480
I, as well.
It's not really fair if I don't.

42:15.700 --> 42:19.410
It says they need models,
no experience necessary.

42:21.530 --> 42:23.620
Hey, want to come with me?

42:23.620 --> 42:26.210
No. I know what I want to do.

42:26.210 --> 42:29.630
OK. What about you?

42:30.460 --> 42:32.710
What do I want to do?

42:34.920 --> 42:36.380
That.

42:38.130 --> 42:40.800
HELP WANTED

42:56.360 --> 42:59.820
- Good. You start today.
- Sir!

43:01.700 --> 43:04.080
There, there.

43:04.080 --> 43:07.120
So have you taken care
of babies?

43:08.160 --> 43:10.250
Kind of. I cared for a bunny.

43:10.580 --> 43:12.710
JOIN THE TEAM!

43:10.580 --> 43:12.710
YOU WILL BE THE STAR!

43:13.960 --> 43:15.340
All right.

43:17.970 --> 43:20.260
- Keep up the good work.
- I can't do it.

43:20.260 --> 43:22.180
Out of the way. Coming through.

43:22.180 --> 43:24.720
- Take those to the docks.
- OK.

43:26.220 --> 43:28.020
All right. Let's keep it moving.

43:28.020 --> 43:29.770
- You can do it.
- Thank you.

43:29.770 --> 43:31.770
You're not paid to sit around.

43:35.190 --> 43:36.730
Excuse me.

43:36.730 --> 43:40.410
Yeah? You can get anything
from baby bottles to rockets

43:40.410 --> 43:42.160
here at Ink's Shop.

43:42.160 --> 43:43.910
I'm here for the job.

43:43.910 --> 43:45.660
Oh, the listing.

43:47.080 --> 43:49.500
- You an Earthling?
- Yes.

43:49.500 --> 43:51.330
Go, go, go, go!

43:51.330 --> 43:53.840
Moon Crestar is in the lead
in this race, what speed,

43:53.840 --> 43:55.800
but Hammer King
is nipping at his heels.

43:55.800 --> 43:59.590
- It's a dead heat.
- Come on! Go, go, go, go!

43:59.590 --> 44:02.760
I was told all flights to
and from Earth were cancelled.

44:02.760 --> 44:06.560
So I'm lucky to meet you.
Can I have your autograph?

44:07.970 --> 44:09.980
You know, as proof
of our meeting.

44:11.190 --> 44:14.310
- You sure you want my autograph.
Yes, please.

44:15.230 --> 44:17.320
OK.

44:20.860 --> 44:23.990
So you guys have books
about the wonders of space, too?

44:24.780 --> 44:26.620
We have lots and lots.

44:28.830 --> 44:31.160
Thanks for using our services.

44:42.300 --> 44:45.470
Maybe it's better if I just
join Kiyoshi at his job.

44:45.470 --> 44:48.010
Noriko!

44:48.890 --> 44:50.730
Don't I look cool?

44:50.730 --> 44:52.730
Hey, watch. Check this out.

44:54.230 --> 44:56.230
Nuts!

44:56.230 --> 45:00.780
Hello, ladies and gentlealiens.
Welcome to "The Space Show."

45:00.780 --> 45:05.450
Third? Why can't you run faster?
Why don't you go faster?

45:05.450 --> 45:07.280
Go, go,go!

45:07.280 --> 45:09.080
What's the matter
with that thing?

45:09.080 --> 45:10.830
Run, run, run, run, run!

45:10.830 --> 45:14.330
Oh, come on!
I don't believe this!

45:22.880 --> 45:25.430
Do you need me to feed you?

45:35.770 --> 45:38.310
Please don't cry.

45:40.110 --> 45:43.070
You're good with animals.

45:45.400 --> 45:47.110
Why are you here?

45:47.110 --> 45:48.780
We came to check on you.

45:48.780 --> 45:51.910
- How's your job?
- I'm still picking one.

45:54.410 --> 45:55.960
Guess what happened.

46:00.250 --> 46:02.840
- I got myself fired.
- What?

46:02.840 --> 46:04.920
That's not even the worst part.

46:06.630 --> 46:08.970
I also owe them a lot of money.

46:10.470 --> 46:12.640
- You dummy!
- I know.

46:13.810 --> 46:16.230
Maybe I should look after
babies, too.

46:16.230 --> 46:17.560
I'm sorry.

46:17.560 --> 46:20.400
I mean, I've taken care
of animals before.

46:23.530 --> 46:25.360
Don't!

46:27.610 --> 46:30.910
It's OK, little guy.

46:32.160 --> 46:35.660
I know she was loud and scary.

46:39.460 --> 46:42.920
I wonder if they think
I'm a screw-up.

46:45.590 --> 46:49.140
So which space wonder
is your favorite, Ink?

46:49.140 --> 46:51.010
Well, this one.

46:53.390 --> 46:55.310
"Pet Star."

46:55.310 --> 46:56.730
Would you like to see it?

46:56.730 --> 46:58.480
- Of course.
- Me, too.

46:58.480 --> 47:00.150
It would be
like a dream come true.

47:00.150 --> 47:02.650
Hey, I could use
some help here.

47:04.610 --> 47:06.440
Why don't you go help?

47:07.780 --> 47:10.620
And be sure to ask my dad
about the Pet Star, OK?

47:10.620 --> 47:12.490
He knows a lot more about it.

47:12.490 --> 47:13.990
OK.

47:16.000 --> 47:18.960
Well, the Pet Star
is like a treasure box.

47:18.960 --> 47:20.880
In fact, it's full
of so much treasure,

47:20.880 --> 47:22.710
you could buy a galaxy with it.

47:22.710 --> 47:24.590
What kind of treasure is in it?

47:24.590 --> 47:26.670
That's part of what makes it
a mystery.

47:26.670 --> 47:29.430
See, explorers and researchers
have been searching for it

47:29.430 --> 47:31.800
for ages but turning up nothing.

47:31.800 --> 47:34.430
Some say it has vanished
to another dimension,

47:34.430 --> 47:37.680
but I still believe
it's in this universe.

47:43.730 --> 47:45.520
See if you can lift that.

47:45.520 --> 47:47.440
OK.

47:47.440 --> 47:48.950
If I found the Pet Star,

47:48.950 --> 47:52.030
then I'd finally be able
to fix this piece of junk.

47:56.740 --> 47:58.540
You doing OK?

47:58.540 --> 48:00.330
Yep. I'm great.

48:33.820 --> 48:37.240
Zughaan!

48:41.620 --> 48:44.920
You, I'll buy those off you.
Please.

48:44.920 --> 48:48.420
I'll pay you anything you want.
How about this much?

48:48.420 --> 48:50.670
Me, too.
I'll buy them off of you.

48:55.300 --> 48:59.390
We can't get to Earth.
So now what do we do?

48:59.390 --> 49:01.600
I must have Zughaan
on the brain.

49:01.600 --> 49:03.850
I keep thinking I hear
someone say it.

49:03.850 --> 49:05.230
Me, too.

49:05.230 --> 49:07.690
Look. It's Zughaan, over there.

49:09.480 --> 49:10.820
Where?

49:11.740 --> 49:14.320
Here. Thanks for your purchase.

49:14.320 --> 49:15.740
You're right.

49:15.740 --> 49:17.280
Yes!

49:23.460 --> 49:25.120
This is so cool.

49:25.120 --> 49:27.540
Isn't it? Shut it off.

49:27.540 --> 49:28.920
Right.

49:32.010 --> 49:34.510
I going to install this engine
in new spaceships

49:34.510 --> 49:36.050
and try to sell them.

49:36.050 --> 49:38.350
If it hits big,
I'll be one rich guy.

49:39.810 --> 49:41.640
Hold that up for me again.

49:41.640 --> 49:43.180
Got it.

49:45.020 --> 49:46.520
That's it.

49:46.520 --> 49:48.980
I'll let you ride this baby
once it's complete.

49:48.980 --> 49:50.520
OK.

49:50.520 --> 49:55.280
I'll be the first
second grader from Earth

49:55.280 --> 49:59.620
who is building a rocket.

49:59.620 --> 50:01.490
OK. You can let go now.

50:05.410 --> 50:07.170
Sorry.

50:07.170 --> 50:09.880
Sometimes my dad
doesn't know when to stop.

50:11.130 --> 50:13.300
That's OK.

50:14.840 --> 50:17.380
You'll feel better once you
drink this special Ink Juice.

50:17.380 --> 50:19.930
Here.

50:27.480 --> 50:28.810
Ink...

50:30.440 --> 50:33.690
The store, is it a spaceship?

50:33.690 --> 50:35.900
Yeah. It's my dad's ship.

50:43.830 --> 50:47.500
Dad and I are traveling through
space with this map as a guide.

50:48.620 --> 50:50.170
What's the dot?

50:50.170 --> 50:53.090
That stands for a big event,
like a festival or race.

50:53.090 --> 50:55.300
Sometimes there'll be
tens of billions

50:55.300 --> 50:57.380
of people there at once.

50:57.380 --> 51:00.640
My dream is to be able
to buy a spacecraft of my own

51:00.640 --> 51:03.010
so I can go to all those events.

51:08.770 --> 51:12.150
"Close Encounters
of the Third Kind."

51:12.150 --> 51:14.820
This is nice.

51:16.820 --> 51:18.820
You guys did really good today.

51:20.610 --> 51:22.780
OK. Let's see
how much money we made.

51:27.200 --> 51:29.120
113 pods.

51:29.120 --> 51:30.710
That's actually pretty good.

51:32.540 --> 51:34.750
We worked hard.

51:37.170 --> 51:40.130
This is how much I made today.

51:41.640 --> 51:45.350
- Those are really little.
- I'll do better tomorrow, OK?

51:47.600 --> 51:49.690
Those coins.

51:49.690 --> 51:51.310
Something wrong with them?

51:51.310 --> 51:55.480
These are commemorative coins,
each worth 20 grand.

51:55.480 --> 51:57.320
These are 5 and 10 grand.

51:57.320 --> 52:00.070
All together, it's 110,000 pods.

52:00.070 --> 52:02.070
All that for some wasabi.

52:03.320 --> 52:05.030
- Wasabi?
- You sold them?

52:05.030 --> 52:06.990
Wasabi is valuable.

52:06.990 --> 52:10.210
Don't worry. I still have
some for us, though. See?

52:10.210 --> 52:12.330
Zughaan!

52:14.040 --> 52:16.590
Natsuki, that's Zughaan
you're holding.

52:18.260 --> 52:19.970
Zughaan?

52:21.220 --> 52:23.220
Does that mean I'm gonna
go to space jail?

52:23.220 --> 52:25.510
You didn't steal it,
so you should be fine.

52:28.970 --> 52:32.020
It's probably best if you
stop selling them, though.

52:32.020 --> 52:35.650
That way, you won't draw
any unnecessary attention.

52:35.650 --> 52:38.110
This is quite a bit of money.

52:38.110 --> 52:41.450
I guess that explains
the poachers.

52:41.450 --> 52:43.610
But now with this money--

52:43.610 --> 52:45.780
Yeah. We can take
the Super Express.

52:45.780 --> 52:47.790
- Awesome.
- Goody.

52:47.790 --> 52:49.660
What a relief.

52:50.830 --> 52:52.790
So no more work, huh?

52:54.630 --> 52:56.590
I guess.

52:59.840 --> 53:02.050
Master, we have good news.

53:02.050 --> 53:03.470
Finally.

53:03.470 --> 53:05.550
We found someone with Zughaan.

53:05.550 --> 53:07.260
Are you positive?

53:07.260 --> 53:09.680
We'll send you the data
right now.

53:10.600 --> 53:12.730
It's an Earthling who had it.

53:12.730 --> 53:16.020
We're gonna grab it
as soon as we get the chance.

53:21.440 --> 53:25.200
So we got to say
good-bye already, huh?

53:25.200 --> 53:30.040
Sorry. I was really planning on
helping you finish your rocket.

53:30.040 --> 53:33.500
Well, unexpected things
happen here in space.

53:33.500 --> 53:35.540
You have a safe trip, OK?

53:36.250 --> 53:38.000
Thanks.

53:38.000 --> 53:39.590
Ink, come here.

53:40.920 --> 53:46.140
Just leave your tears
in the park

53:49.680 --> 53:51.060
Here.

53:54.940 --> 53:56.850
For me?

53:56.850 --> 54:00.320
While we travel, we're going
to visit all those spots.

54:00.320 --> 54:03.990
So maybe there's a chance
we'll meet again.

54:11.370 --> 54:13.660
WONDERS OF SPACE

54:12.120 --> 54:13.790
This is for you.

55:10.800 --> 55:12.760
Hi.

55:12.760 --> 55:14.970
Here you go.

55:14.970 --> 55:17.890
Take my hand.

56:22.750 --> 56:25.130
The moon sure was fun,
wasn't it?

56:25.130 --> 56:26.880
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

56:39.270 --> 56:40.890
It's better this way.

56:40.890 --> 56:42.850
Now it's like a real train.

56:42.850 --> 56:46.650
I know.
This is the best field trip.

56:46.650 --> 56:49.490
Looks like somebody
got their wish.

56:49.490 --> 56:54.280
Sliced meteor. Space water
and other snacks for sale.

56:54.280 --> 56:57.950
- Over here, please.
- Yeah. We'll buy them all.

56:57.950 --> 57:01.120
- Wait a minute.
- What's wrong?

57:01.120 --> 57:03.170
It's not like we don't
have money.

57:03.170 --> 57:05.420
We had to pay off your debt.

57:07.630 --> 57:09.670
We have nothing left?

57:10.630 --> 57:13.720
Well, we do have a little bit.

57:13.720 --> 57:15.260
Really?

57:17.050 --> 57:19.890
The train will make
super speed jump shortly.

57:19.890 --> 57:21.560
All passengers,
please remain seated...

57:21.560 --> 57:23.100
What's super speed?

57:23.100 --> 57:24.850
It's faster than light speed.

57:26.360 --> 57:28.440
Faster than light speed?

57:36.030 --> 57:38.330
It's another star system.

57:38.330 --> 57:41.120
So then where are we?

57:47.670 --> 57:51.460
M45--the Pleiades star cluster.

57:51.460 --> 57:54.510
We just traveled
400 light years.

57:54.510 --> 57:57.970
This stop is Planet Picha-Picha.

57:57.970 --> 58:00.600
The train bound for Milla
is scheduled to depart

58:00.600 --> 58:03.810
from deck number 15 in 6 months.

58:03.810 --> 58:06.400
- So you all are from Earth?
- That's right.

58:06.400 --> 58:08.690
We'll wait
till the next station.

58:08.690 --> 58:10.610
Good idea.

58:10.610 --> 58:12.820
Right. Thanks.

58:16.360 --> 58:19.200
This is the fifth
most delicious food in space.

58:19.200 --> 58:21.410
It's only sold
at the next station.

58:21.410 --> 58:22.790
- Let's get it.
- Let's get it.

58:22.790 --> 58:24.160
Yeah.

58:24.160 --> 58:26.000
- Can we, please, Pochi?
- Can we, please, Pochi?

58:27.830 --> 58:29.750
Just this once.

58:40.890 --> 58:43.020
There's a limit of 3 per person.

58:43.020 --> 58:45.140
Whoever gets back first wins.

58:45.140 --> 58:47.520
You are on.

58:51.940 --> 58:53.690
- Go!
- Go!

58:56.900 --> 58:58.780
Heavy.

58:58.780 --> 59:01.740
I can't move.

59:01.740 --> 59:04.450
It's best not to lie around.

59:11.420 --> 59:12.960
Thank you.

59:12.960 --> 59:14.760
- Thank you.
- No worries.

59:14.760 --> 59:17.800
When you help others,
you help yourself.

59:24.510 --> 59:26.850
The Duke of Mahal
is an eccentric fella.

59:26.850 --> 59:29.600
He refuses to install
gravity antennas.

59:29.600 --> 59:33.270
It's a shame,
but space is quite vast.

59:33.270 --> 59:36.690
You'll find many other kinds
of delicious food.

59:38.990 --> 59:40.660
That host from "The Space Show."

59:40.660 --> 59:43.870
Yeah. I've been following them
for a while.

59:43.870 --> 59:47.120
Wait, but can't you watch it
from anywhere?

59:48.460 --> 59:51.540
I want to get as close
as possible.

59:51.540 --> 59:55.300
I'm really interested in seeing
how they create the show.

59:55.300 --> 59:57.590
But what about your job?

59:57.590 --> 59:59.470
Luckily, this is my work.

59:59.470 --> 01:00:02.260
I sell info about the show
to fans.

01:00:02.260 --> 01:00:06.180
You know who's a hardcore fan?
The Duke of Mahal.

01:00:08.730 --> 01:00:10.770
"The Space Show"
travels so fast,

01:00:10.770 --> 01:00:12.270
it's impossible to catch.

01:00:12.270 --> 01:00:14.690
So I anticipate where it'll be
and wait.

01:00:16.230 --> 01:00:18.070
Where's it gonna be next?

01:00:19.190 --> 01:00:21.280
- That's a secret.
- What?

01:00:21.280 --> 01:00:23.570
If you pay me, I'll tell you.

01:00:24.990 --> 01:00:28.040
Our friend Pochi right there
is a friend of Marie's.

01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:29.450
Is that true?

01:00:31.250 --> 01:00:33.920
I'm from the same planet as her.
That's all.

01:00:34.960 --> 01:00:36.590
I thought you knew her.

01:00:36.590 --> 01:00:38.170
Well, that's too bad.

01:00:38.170 --> 01:00:40.380
Here's my card
if you ever change your mind.

01:00:40.380 --> 01:00:42.550
Name is Goba.
You can call my shop.

01:00:59.400 --> 01:01:02.530
I never dreamed
you could be like this.

01:01:02.530 --> 01:01:04.570
You're a coward.

01:01:04.570 --> 01:01:06.660
You're wrong.

01:01:06.660 --> 01:01:10.750
I'm disappointed in you, Pochi.

01:01:10.750 --> 01:01:13.670
You've got it all wrong.

01:01:17.340 --> 01:01:19.630
Let me explain.

01:01:26.010 --> 01:01:31.680
Yes. I love it. I love it,
but I want it more dynamic.

01:01:32.850 --> 01:01:35.850
Good.
One more time from the top.

01:01:39.440 --> 01:01:41.740
You're in a good mood today.

01:01:42.860 --> 01:01:44.530
You know why.

01:01:44.530 --> 01:01:47.450
This is going to be
our biggest show yet.

01:01:51.620 --> 01:01:55.370
Can't we stay like this
happily ever after?

01:01:55.370 --> 01:01:58.000
He and I
have unfinished business.

01:02:02.630 --> 01:02:03.970
Attention, all passengers.

01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:05.970
The train will be
temporarily delayed.

01:02:05.970 --> 01:02:07.760
What's going on?

01:02:07.760 --> 01:02:11.970
It's just traffic.
The tunnel is always congested.

01:02:15.480 --> 01:02:17.600
It's glowing.

01:02:18.770 --> 01:02:21.900
Why is there a tunnel
in space, anyway?

01:02:22.900 --> 01:02:24.740
Yeah. Why, Pochi?

01:02:24.740 --> 01:02:26.570
Got to use the restroom.

01:02:27.320 --> 01:02:29.030
This area is dangerous.

01:02:30.240 --> 01:02:32.450
That up there
is the Dark Triangle.

01:02:33.870 --> 01:02:36.460
You can only get through it
by using that tunnel.

01:02:37.330 --> 01:02:39.540
What's the Dark Triangle?

01:02:39.540 --> 01:02:42.460
It's a nebula
made of antimatter.

01:02:42.460 --> 01:02:46.090
Those flashes
are annihilation explosions.

01:02:51.720 --> 01:02:53.270
Amazing.

01:02:53.270 --> 01:02:56.850
Doesn't look like we'll
be moving any time soon.

01:02:59.440 --> 01:03:01.480
Can we really make it
back home in time?

01:03:01.480 --> 01:03:04.150
There've just been so many
unscheduled delays.

01:03:04.150 --> 01:03:07.450
Don't worry about it.
That's how things are in space.

01:03:07.450 --> 01:03:09.360
Yeah, but--

01:03:12.910 --> 01:03:15.580
Relax. There's no need
to get worked up.

01:03:15.580 --> 01:03:18.500
I'll make sure everything

01:03:15.580 --> 01:03:18.500
works itself out, OK?

01:03:29.380 --> 01:03:31.430
Are you all right?

01:03:39.600 --> 01:03:42.480
I'm just worried
about getting us home.

01:03:42.480 --> 01:03:45.730
Stuff keeps happening
that changes our plans.

01:03:48.990 --> 01:03:51.450
You guys are my responsibility.

01:03:51.450 --> 01:03:54.030
So if we get stuck here,
it's my fault.

01:03:54.030 --> 01:03:55.830
Don't think that way.

01:03:55.830 --> 01:03:58.120
We're having a lot of fun,
and none of us think

01:03:58.120 --> 01:04:01.000
any of this is your fault.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:04.340
I still feel guilty.

01:04:24.150 --> 01:04:26.520
Attention, all passengers.

01:04:26.520 --> 01:04:29.030
This is the Space
Control Center.

01:04:29.030 --> 01:04:32.030
We're currently experiencing
8-hour delays.

01:04:32.030 --> 01:04:34.780
Do they have records on
the birth of the universe here?

01:04:34.780 --> 01:04:37.950
Sure. I imagine someone
would keep a record.

01:04:37.950 --> 01:04:39.790
I wish I could get off here.

01:04:39.790 --> 01:04:41.500
You don't want the train
to leave without you, though.

01:04:41.500 --> 01:04:43.460
- You're right.
- I've waited a long time.

01:04:43.460 --> 01:04:46.380
I refuse to wait any longer.
What a waste of time.

01:04:46.380 --> 01:04:48.960
Pochi, did you see that?
The tadpole spoke.

01:04:48.960 --> 01:04:50.920
I'm not here.

01:04:50.920 --> 01:04:54.180
Pochi? Pochi?

01:04:54.180 --> 01:04:56.140
Pochi, it's you, isn't it?

01:04:56.140 --> 01:04:57.470
Sorry, wrong guy.

01:04:57.470 --> 01:05:00.180
Don't play dumb with me.
You got my money.

01:05:00.180 --> 01:05:04.270
Oh, I'm sorry.
Did I scare you guys?

01:05:04.270 --> 01:05:05.730
I'm Tony.

01:05:05.730 --> 01:05:07.980
I work here
at the Space Control Center,

01:05:07.980 --> 01:05:10.110
and this is my pet Johnny.

01:05:10.110 --> 01:05:12.320
Nice to meet you.

01:05:12.320 --> 01:05:16.870
You're the first Earthlings to
ever travel this far in space.

01:05:16.870 --> 01:05:18.990
So did Pochi kidnap you?

01:05:20.200 --> 01:05:21.540
That is absurd!

01:05:24.370 --> 01:05:25.750
No, no!

01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:27.500
I've known Pochi for years,

01:05:27.500 --> 01:05:29.920
and he's always getting
others into trouble.

01:05:31.420 --> 01:05:34.720
I went ahead and sent a report
of your visit to the Center.

01:05:34.720 --> 01:05:36.720
We're keeping records
of everyone

01:05:36.720 --> 01:05:38.390
and everything in space.

01:05:38.390 --> 01:05:41.640
So do you have any information
on how the universe began?

01:05:41.640 --> 01:05:43.810
You should inquire about that
with the Center.

01:05:43.810 --> 01:05:46.520
I'm only in charge of records.

01:05:48.900 --> 01:05:51.070
What are you investigating now?

01:05:51.070 --> 01:05:52.490
Top secret.

01:05:52.490 --> 01:05:54.990
Why is it so top secret?

01:05:54.990 --> 01:05:58.370
You're cute,
so I'll make an exception, OK?

01:05:58.370 --> 01:06:00.040
There are rumors
that someone is selling

01:06:00.040 --> 01:06:02.540
a plant called Zughaan
on the black market.

01:06:03.830 --> 01:06:06.080
According to our records,
it should be extinct,

01:06:06.080 --> 01:06:08.130
hence the investigation.

01:06:10.880 --> 01:06:13.420
Well, good luck with that.

01:06:16.970 --> 01:06:18.850
We'll take the bus from here.
See you.

01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:20.890
- Thanks a lot. Bye.
- Thanks a lot. Bye.

01:06:20.890 --> 01:06:23.310
Next time,
you better have my money.

01:06:38.990 --> 01:06:41.990
It's OK. Trip is almost over.

01:07:10.860 --> 01:07:13.320
This is
the Royal Kenbritte University,

01:07:13.320 --> 01:07:15.490
the education center
of the planet.

01:07:15.490 --> 01:07:16.990
What are we doing here?

01:07:16.990 --> 01:07:18.820
Filling out forms
to go to Earth.

01:07:18.820 --> 01:07:20.660
So do you go to school here?

01:07:20.660 --> 01:07:23.910
- Well--
- Welcome back, Professor.

01:07:23.910 --> 01:07:26.790
- Oh, good afternoon.
- Professor?

01:07:34.710 --> 01:07:36.630
He's a professor?

01:07:37.760 --> 01:07:39.220
Yeah.

01:07:41.720 --> 01:07:45.390
He did say
he was doing research.

01:07:58.650 --> 01:08:01.450
- So, Amane...
- What?

01:08:01.450 --> 01:08:03.530
When we get home,
you want to go into town?

01:08:03.530 --> 01:08:04.870
How come?

01:08:06.370 --> 01:08:08.450
Well, the thing is--

01:08:13.130 --> 01:08:15.630
- Thief!
- We got it.

01:08:21.340 --> 01:08:22.760
Over there.

01:08:22.760 --> 01:08:24.430
Hey, stop!

01:08:35.190 --> 01:08:37.320
We got the Zughaan.

01:08:39.490 --> 01:08:41.490
They're still there.

01:08:41.490 --> 01:08:43.200
- Bomb, please.
- Here.

01:08:47.040 --> 01:08:49.540
Yes. Let's go.

01:08:51.160 --> 01:08:52.750
No!

01:08:56.920 --> 01:08:59.420
Hey, you need a lift, Professor?

01:08:59.420 --> 01:09:01.340
Can't you go faster?

01:09:01.340 --> 01:09:03.800
They're right behind us.
Leave us alone.

01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:05.180
Get out of the way.

01:09:05.180 --> 01:09:06.600
- They're there.
- I see them.

01:09:06.600 --> 01:09:08.810
- Go faster.
- Go. Go.

01:09:11.850 --> 01:09:14.560
- Can you ram into them?
- Of course.

01:09:30.580 --> 01:09:32.250
So cool.

01:09:35.040 --> 01:09:37.420
He's the same guy
we saw on Earth.

01:09:37.420 --> 01:09:38.920
So we meet again.

01:09:38.920 --> 01:09:41.050
I was gonna say that.

01:09:41.050 --> 01:09:42.880
It's no use. Surrender.

01:09:44.220 --> 01:09:45.550
Watch it.

01:09:55.100 --> 01:09:57.270
Let go! Get off!

01:09:57.270 --> 01:09:59.110
Whoa!

01:10:22.210 --> 01:10:24.920
Professor, we found this
on the suspects.

01:10:24.920 --> 01:10:26.760
Do they look familiar?

01:10:26.760 --> 01:10:29.600
It's in the ancient
Sombrero alphabet.

01:10:29.600 --> 01:10:33.020
I think it says "God."

01:10:34.310 --> 01:10:35.810
May I borrow this?

01:10:37.270 --> 01:10:39.310
Your flight leaves
the day after tomorrow

01:10:39.310 --> 01:10:40.900
in the morning.

01:10:40.900 --> 01:10:42.280
You can stay at my house
until then.

01:10:42.280 --> 01:10:44.400
- Yay!
- Yay!

01:10:57.290 --> 01:10:58.670
Please, come on in.

01:10:58.670 --> 01:11:00.340
Wow!

01:11:00.340 --> 01:11:01.710
Whoa!

01:11:06.420 --> 01:11:08.890
Do you live here
by yourself?

01:11:08.890 --> 01:11:11.050
No. It's my parents' house.

01:11:12.310 --> 01:11:14.020
Hey, that's Neppo!

01:11:14.020 --> 01:11:15.430
And Marie, too!

01:11:15.430 --> 01:11:19.190
Hmm...so you are friends
with Marie and Neppo.

01:11:19.190 --> 01:11:23.440
Yeah. We worked in the same lab
a long time ago.

01:11:25.320 --> 01:11:28.360
Oh, Pochi, welcome home.

01:11:28.360 --> 01:11:29.990
Good to be home.

01:11:29.990 --> 01:11:31.740
Oh, we have guests.

01:11:31.740 --> 01:11:32.990
Welcome, all of you.

01:11:32.990 --> 01:11:36.580
- Thank you for having us.
- Yeah, thanks.

01:11:36.580 --> 01:11:41.130
Thank you very much
for saving our son's life.

01:11:41.130 --> 01:11:43.840
We just did what
we thought was right.

01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:47.010
Wow! I heard Earth
was remote and wild,

01:11:47.010 --> 01:11:49.300
but you are quite civilized.

01:11:49.300 --> 01:11:52.010
There's no need
to be so polite.

01:11:52.010 --> 01:11:53.600
Go on, start eating.

01:11:53.600 --> 01:11:55.310
- Bon Appetit!
- Bon Appetit!

01:11:55.310 --> 01:11:58.390
My mother's cake is
the best in this world.

01:11:58.390 --> 01:12:00.190
Mmmm!

01:12:00.190 --> 01:12:02.610
Mmm! Delicious!

01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:05.400
I'm so delighted
that you like it.

01:12:05.400 --> 01:12:07.320
How do you make it?

01:12:07.320 --> 01:12:09.320
I'll show you how later
if you want.

01:12:09.320 --> 01:12:12.030
- Yes, please.
- Teach me, too!

01:12:12.030 --> 01:12:14.280
Me, too!

01:12:17.200 --> 01:12:20.250
Well, I have patients
to attend to,

01:12:20.250 --> 01:12:21.830
so if you'll excuse me...

01:12:21.830 --> 01:12:25.250
Do you have
your own clinic?

01:12:25.250 --> 01:12:27.000
Yes.

01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:29.670
Would you mind
if I had a look?

01:12:31.010 --> 01:12:33.970
There are many rare
diseases in space.

01:12:33.970 --> 01:12:36.430
My father uses what he's
learned from archaeology

01:12:36.430 --> 01:12:38.350
to treat his patients.

01:12:38.350 --> 01:12:41.980
It's called ancient
biotherapeutics.

01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:45.770
It uses plant vitality
to rejuvenate one's life force.

01:12:45.770 --> 01:12:49.400
When she came to me, her whole
body used to be petrified.

01:12:49.400 --> 01:12:51.070
She's doing much better now.

01:12:51.070 --> 01:12:52.450
Oh!

01:12:52.450 --> 01:12:55.160
You're doing great.
Just hang in there, Clara.

01:12:55.160 --> 01:12:58.410
Your voice will
come back real soon.

01:12:58.410 --> 01:13:01.540
You did great.
So brave.

01:13:03.000 --> 01:13:06.040
Next, I'm going to plant
a seed right here.

01:13:06.040 --> 01:13:08.550
Now try to sit up, OK?

01:13:12.430 --> 01:13:14.260
I'm happy to help out.

01:13:14.260 --> 01:13:17.720
Mmm, just like that.

01:13:17.720 --> 01:13:19.060
Bah!

01:13:19.060 --> 01:13:21.890
That's not right.

01:13:21.890 --> 01:13:24.230
Buhh!

01:13:24.230 --> 01:13:26.270
Don't worry, girls.
You'll get it.

01:13:36.740 --> 01:13:39.580
This could be
an incredible discovery.

01:13:41.080 --> 01:13:43.370
I wonder if it
really is Zughaan...

01:13:43.370 --> 01:13:46.580
or perhaps it's just a plant
that's very similar.

01:13:53.590 --> 01:13:55.470
We'll have results tomorrow.

01:13:55.470 --> 01:13:58.550
The rumors about the existence
of Zughaan are spreading.

01:13:58.550 --> 01:14:02.480
I had a run-in with
some poachers on Earth.

01:14:02.480 --> 01:14:04.940
It was the same poachers
who attacked us in town.

01:14:04.940 --> 01:14:07.900
- And this?
- It was on the suspects.

01:14:07.900 --> 01:14:12.070
- Hmm. Ancient
Sombrero alphabet, huh?

01:14:12.070 --> 01:14:14.610
Didn't you do
a study on this?

01:14:17.320 --> 01:14:20.490
Earth is somewhere
around there.

01:14:20.490 --> 01:14:23.500
We sure are a long way
from home, huh?

01:14:23.500 --> 01:14:27.250
21 million light years,
to be exact.

01:14:32.170 --> 01:14:34.170
That's hard to wrap
your head around.

01:14:34.170 --> 01:14:36.090
Yeah.

01:14:36.090 --> 01:14:39.300
What do you think
they're doing back home?

01:14:39.300 --> 01:14:40.720
You getting homesick?

01:14:40.720 --> 01:14:43.600
Mmm...I'm not!

01:14:47.440 --> 01:14:50.650
We'll be back on Earth
the day after tomorrow.

01:15:20.550 --> 01:15:24.770
Aah! I'm sorry!

01:15:49.210 --> 01:15:52.210
We're soaking wet!

01:15:52.210 --> 01:15:54.800
Man, it started pouring
out of the blue.

01:15:54.800 --> 01:15:56.590
Here's today's forecast.

01:15:56.590 --> 01:15:59.630
Get ready for a beautiful day
in the Inland Empires

01:15:59.630 --> 01:16:01.220
with lots of sunshine.

01:16:01.220 --> 01:16:03.260
A small lingering
low-pressure system

01:16:03.260 --> 01:16:04.640
will create gusts of wind,

01:16:04.640 --> 01:16:07.890
so please watch out
for unexpected wind storms.

01:16:15.570 --> 01:16:18.110
I hate you!
I hate you!

01:16:20.360 --> 01:16:23.370
- Uhh!
- Amane, wait!

01:16:26.830 --> 01:16:28.660
You guys fighting?

01:16:28.660 --> 01:16:31.210
Hmm?

01:16:31.210 --> 01:16:32.750
Not exactly.

01:16:34.210 --> 01:16:37.000
I think I'll get her
another rabbit anyway.

01:16:38.760 --> 01:16:42.260
Because if I don't do that,
she'll never forgive me.

01:16:42.260 --> 01:16:44.850
You really think that?

01:16:52.690 --> 01:16:54.730
Huh?

01:16:56.940 --> 01:16:58.980
- Natsuki.

01:16:58.980 --> 01:17:00.650
Yeah?

01:17:00.650 --> 01:17:03.070
What if Amane
happened to go missing?

01:17:03.070 --> 01:17:05.070
- Huh?
- Pretend.

01:17:05.070 --> 01:17:07.200
Just imagine someone
said to you,

01:17:07.200 --> 01:17:09.700
"Don't worry. I'll just go
and find you another kid."

01:17:09.700 --> 01:17:11.580
Ah, how could you?

01:17:11.580 --> 01:17:14.670
You can't just replace Amane.
It wouldn't be the same!

01:17:14.670 --> 01:17:16.710
How could you even
suggest something like that?

01:17:16.710 --> 01:17:18.300
What about Pyon-Kichi?

01:17:21.420 --> 01:17:23.260
But, I...

01:17:23.260 --> 01:17:27.350
I don't...I mean,
what do I do?

01:17:27.350 --> 01:17:29.720
You need to apologize.

01:17:29.720 --> 01:17:33.350
But I did many times.

01:17:33.350 --> 01:17:36.400
And all those times
you apologized to her,

01:17:36.400 --> 01:17:38.860
did you know
why you were wrong?

01:17:44.700 --> 01:17:46.660
Do you know what makes
a great hero?

01:17:46.660 --> 01:17:49.330
It's because
they have courage.

01:17:49.330 --> 01:17:52.040
To admit you're wrong
and acknowledge your mistakes,

01:17:52.040 --> 01:17:54.370
well, that takes
a lot of courage,

01:17:54.370 --> 01:17:56.830
and that is nothing
to be embarrassed about.

01:17:59.670 --> 01:18:01.630
Why don't you
go make up with her?

01:18:01.630 --> 01:18:05.010
Why should I? Besides,
we're not fighting.

01:18:06.510 --> 01:18:09.850
But you're still upset about
the Pyon-Kichi thing, right?

01:18:11.350 --> 01:18:14.060
So, what do you want
Natsuki to do?

01:18:15.390 --> 01:18:16.850
Hmm?

01:18:20.610 --> 01:18:24.240
I just want her to be
like she used to be.

01:18:24.240 --> 01:18:26.280
You mean, she didn't
used to be like this?

01:18:26.280 --> 01:18:27.780
She's totally different.

01:18:27.780 --> 01:18:31.370
When she used to come visit,
she was way more normal.

01:18:31.370 --> 01:18:34.330
She was sloppy.
She wasn't a show-off.

01:18:34.330 --> 01:18:36.750
But ever since she moved in,

01:18:36.750 --> 01:18:39.380
she just suddenly
became really bossy.

01:18:39.380 --> 01:18:42.340
And whenever we play,
instead of being fun,

01:18:42.340 --> 01:18:44.260
it's like a favor.

01:18:46.430 --> 01:18:48.640
And about Pyon-Kichi...

01:18:48.640 --> 01:18:51.510
of course I really
miss him and all,

01:18:51.510 --> 01:18:54.770
but I don't want Natsuki
to buy me another rabbit.

01:18:54.770 --> 01:18:57.350
Pyon-Kichi
is his own rabbit.

01:18:57.350 --> 01:19:02.360
He doesn't belong to me
or anyone else.

01:19:02.360 --> 01:19:04.820
Well, why don't you tell her
exactly how you feel?

01:19:04.820 --> 01:19:07.240
Huh? What if...

01:19:07.240 --> 01:19:08.780
It'll be fine,

01:19:08.780 --> 01:19:11.780
and you guys will
make up real quick.

01:19:11.780 --> 01:19:14.700
Isn't that what you want?

01:19:14.700 --> 01:19:17.290
Yeah.

01:19:17.290 --> 01:19:20.420
Just apologize
and remember to be sincere.

01:19:20.420 --> 01:19:23.550
It's OK. Tell her
exactly how you feel.

01:19:25.970 --> 01:19:29.430
Apologize and be sincere.

01:19:29.430 --> 01:19:32.560
Apologize
and just be sincere.

01:19:32.560 --> 01:19:33.970
Oh!

01:19:38.810 --> 01:19:40.560
- Amane.
- Natsuki.

01:19:42.820 --> 01:19:44.570
- Listen.
- Listen.

01:19:52.950 --> 01:19:54.950
You first.

01:19:57.790 --> 01:19:59.580
I wanted to
tell you something.

01:20:03.880 --> 01:20:05.210
Me too.

01:20:08.050 --> 01:20:11.300
Amane...

01:20:11.300 --> 01:20:13.600
I wanted to say that--

01:20:25.650 --> 01:20:26.860
Whoa!

01:20:26.860 --> 01:20:29.360
Iron Mask
has been attacked.

01:20:29.360 --> 01:20:32.360
He's gotten himself out of
plenty of sticky situations,

01:20:32.360 --> 01:20:34.910
but this time,
he's badly hurt.

01:20:34.910 --> 01:20:36.870
His shield has been destroyed.

01:20:36.870 --> 01:20:40.500
The only thing he has left
to rely on is his courage,

01:20:40.500 --> 01:20:42.500
but he is full
of determination.

01:20:42.500 --> 01:20:47.550
And he goes, "I will protect
my loved one at all costs."

01:20:47.550 --> 01:20:49.510
The truth, though,
is that the evil squad

01:20:49.510 --> 01:20:52.800
was actually after
Princess Crystal.

01:20:56.930 --> 01:20:58.350
No!

01:20:58.350 --> 01:21:00.020
Hey!

01:21:29.340 --> 01:21:31.380
What do you mean, there's
no crime scene investigators?

01:21:31.380 --> 01:21:32.680
Where are they?

01:21:32.680 --> 01:21:34.680
I apologize.
They were called away.

01:21:34.680 --> 01:21:37.890
There was a major kidnapping
on Choo-Choo planet.

01:21:37.890 --> 01:21:42.390
There's more. We kinda lost
those 3 guys we arrested.

01:21:42.390 --> 01:21:43.940
But how?

01:21:43.940 --> 01:21:45.520
I'm not really sure.

01:21:45.520 --> 01:21:49.020
They were already gone
before we noticed it.

01:21:56.820 --> 01:21:58.910
Kiyoshi.

01:21:58.910 --> 01:22:01.000
Your guys' flight
back home to Earth--

01:22:01.000 --> 01:22:03.080
It leaves tomorrow morning.

01:22:05.710 --> 01:22:09.090
So, I'll take you
to the airport.

01:22:11.010 --> 01:22:13.050
OK.

01:22:19.760 --> 01:22:21.100
Excuse me.

01:22:25.100 --> 01:22:27.020
Did they tell you anything?

01:22:27.020 --> 01:22:29.020
No.

01:22:29.020 --> 01:22:30.520
I see.

01:22:31.940 --> 01:22:33.990
And what about
your friends?

01:22:33.990 --> 01:22:36.110
They're still outside.

01:22:40.830 --> 01:22:43.500
I'll go fix them
something to eat.

01:22:43.500 --> 01:22:45.120
That would be nice.

01:23:12.900 --> 01:23:15.030
Tomorrow.

01:23:15.030 --> 01:23:18.160
We leave tomorrow
in the morning.

01:23:23.120 --> 01:23:25.370
We'll go back
to the village.

01:23:32.670 --> 01:23:35.050
They were after the Zughaan.

01:23:35.050 --> 01:23:38.180
Amane got taken
by accident...

01:23:41.720 --> 01:23:44.310
and those 3 escaped.

01:23:45.720 --> 01:23:47.640
They followed me
from Earth,

01:23:47.640 --> 01:23:49.190
so they can't be
after money.

01:23:50.980 --> 01:23:55.150
Whoever's behind this
knows the true value of Zughaan.

01:23:58.700 --> 01:24:01.530
You. Could you
have done this?

01:24:01.530 --> 01:24:03.200
Neppo.

01:24:07.750 --> 01:24:10.120
The Zughaan is mine.

01:24:10.120 --> 01:24:11.710
At last!

01:24:37.280 --> 01:24:41.240
What are we supposed to tell
Amane's parents?

01:24:43.240 --> 01:24:45.160
We have to tell them
the truth.

01:24:45.160 --> 01:24:46.870
We have no choice.

01:24:49.450 --> 01:24:51.250
It's all my fault.

01:24:52.710 --> 01:24:54.750
I shouldn't have
brought you here.

01:24:54.750 --> 01:24:57.750
I just got so caught up
in the excitement.

01:24:57.750 --> 01:24:59.880
We never should have
left the village.

01:25:18.820 --> 01:25:20.150
Come on.

01:25:20.150 --> 01:25:21.740
Let's go home.

01:25:21.740 --> 01:25:26.280
You sure do think that's
the right thing to do?

01:25:32.500 --> 01:25:35.960
There's nothing else
we can do.

01:25:35.960 --> 01:25:39.300
Look, I don't know
what'll happen either.

01:25:44.840 --> 01:25:46.850
If I were Amane,

01:25:46.850 --> 01:25:51.230
I think I'd wait for you guys
to come rescue me.

01:25:51.230 --> 01:25:53.140
And you know what,

01:25:53.140 --> 01:25:56.560
I'd want it to be you guys
who came to my rescue,

01:25:56.560 --> 01:26:00.230
because that's what would
make me the most happy.

01:26:00.230 --> 01:26:02.740
I get it. OK?

01:26:05.410 --> 01:26:09.160
But--so, what are we
supposed to do, then?

01:26:09.160 --> 01:26:12.200
I mean, we're just a bunch
of kids, after all.

01:26:12.200 --> 01:26:14.250
Really, how are we
supposed to fight

01:26:14.250 --> 01:26:17.130
against aliens and UFOs?

01:26:17.130 --> 01:26:19.880
I don't know what
we're supposed to do,

01:26:19.880 --> 01:26:22.050
but I know that
we have to do something!

01:26:22.050 --> 01:26:24.340
Stop acting like
you know everything!

01:26:27.680 --> 01:26:29.350
Stop it!

01:26:31.100 --> 01:26:33.350
Please, stop it.

01:26:48.910 --> 01:26:50.450
I agree.

01:26:54.370 --> 01:26:56.790
I've always wanted
to be a superhero

01:26:56.790 --> 01:26:58.540
ever since I was little.

01:27:00.040 --> 01:27:03.920
I'd imagine myself in these
exact types of situations--

01:27:03.920 --> 01:27:05.880
a princess gets kidnapped

01:27:05.880 --> 01:27:07.880
and the hero would
have to risk everything

01:27:07.880 --> 01:27:10.930
to rescue her
from the enemy.

01:27:10.930 --> 01:27:13.390
I thought it was so cool.

01:27:14.810 --> 01:27:19.270
But now, it's really happening,
and I'm so scared.

01:27:19.270 --> 01:27:21.400
I don't know what to do.

01:27:22.770 --> 01:27:25.110
Kiyoshi's right.

01:27:25.110 --> 01:27:28.280
We don't even know
what we're up against,

01:27:28.280 --> 01:27:31.410
so how are we supposed
to know how to help her?

01:27:36.250 --> 01:27:40.830
You know, Amane's probably
even more scared than I am.

01:27:42.210 --> 01:27:44.920
I can't imagine
what she's going through.

01:27:44.920 --> 01:27:48.840
She must feel so
helpless and alone.

01:27:48.840 --> 01:27:50.970
No.

01:27:50.970 --> 01:27:53.430
We have to rescue her.

01:27:54.640 --> 01:27:56.350
I know she would do
the same for us

01:27:56.350 --> 01:27:58.440
if she were in our shoes.

01:27:59.900 --> 01:28:01.360
I'm coming.

01:28:02.940 --> 01:28:04.440
Don't you worry, Amane.

01:28:05.940 --> 01:28:08.820
I promise, I may not
be a hero,

01:28:08.820 --> 01:28:11.950
but it's wrong to
go home without her!

01:28:16.870 --> 01:28:19.460
She's right, Kiyoshi.

01:28:23.500 --> 01:28:26.460
I'll go along with
whatever you decide, OK?

01:28:34.010 --> 01:28:35.600
So, where do we start?

01:28:35.600 --> 01:28:37.770
Mmm, no idea.

01:28:37.770 --> 01:28:39.770
Me neither,
but we'll find her.

01:28:40.980 --> 01:28:43.480
When we do, how do
we get her back?

01:28:45.980 --> 01:28:47.360
We'll figure it out.

01:28:47.360 --> 01:28:50.070
And we'll give it our all.

01:28:52.570 --> 01:28:54.030
Agreed.

01:28:54.030 --> 01:28:56.370
And it doesn't matter
that we don't have a plan.

01:28:56.370 --> 01:28:58.330
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

01:28:58.330 --> 01:29:01.000
Who cares, as long as
we're together?

01:29:01.000 --> 01:29:02.670
- Mmm!
- Mmm!

01:29:02.670 --> 01:29:05.380
We're in this together!

01:29:05.380 --> 01:29:07.630
And no one
gets left behind!

01:29:10.300 --> 01:29:12.340
Professor,
you can't do this!

01:29:12.340 --> 01:29:15.350
I promise to return it
when I'm done.

01:29:15.350 --> 01:29:17.310
I'm gonna have to report you.

01:29:17.310 --> 01:29:19.140
Report away.

01:29:27.480 --> 01:29:30.150
Thank you, Pochi.

01:29:35.200 --> 01:29:38.450
You sure the Space Show
is involved in this?

01:29:38.450 --> 01:29:40.000
Yeah.

01:29:40.000 --> 01:29:42.870
Then why don't you
just tell the police?

01:29:42.870 --> 01:29:44.420
I have no proof.

01:29:44.420 --> 01:29:46.460
Besides, if this
got out to the public,

01:29:46.460 --> 01:29:47.880
Neppo would just flee.

01:29:47.880 --> 01:29:49.920
We should keep this
to ourselves

01:29:49.920 --> 01:29:52.470
until we can rescue Amane.

01:29:52.470 --> 01:29:55.470
Mmm, but what do you think?

01:29:55.470 --> 01:29:56.890
I say we do it!

01:29:56.890 --> 01:29:58.560
Yeah!

01:30:00.720 --> 01:30:02.520
It's a reply from Goba.

01:30:04.020 --> 01:30:07.440
So, where's the Space Show
gonna be next?

01:30:07.440 --> 01:30:09.770
The Great Wall

01:30:09.770 --> 01:30:11.570
at the Space Festival!

01:30:30.090 --> 01:30:32.090
It's so crowded!

01:30:32.090 --> 01:30:34.220
Well, this is
a major event.

01:30:35.880 --> 01:30:38.720
Welcome, all,
to the Space Festival.

01:30:38.720 --> 01:30:41.470
Please remember to secure
all of your belongings.

01:30:41.470 --> 01:30:43.810
We hope you have
a wonderful time!

01:30:43.810 --> 01:30:45.100
Mr. Goba!

01:30:45.100 --> 01:30:46.310
Hmm?

01:30:46.310 --> 01:30:49.810
Ho ho!
You guys made it.

01:30:49.810 --> 01:30:52.480
- Their final broadcast?
- Their final broadcast?

01:30:52.480 --> 01:30:55.490
Yeah. The show issued
an official announcement.

01:30:55.490 --> 01:30:57.820
The whole galaxy
is buzzing about it.

01:30:57.820 --> 01:30:59.280
- Huh?
- Huh?

01:30:59.280 --> 01:31:01.620
We'll use these cameras
to communicate.

01:31:04.500 --> 01:31:07.040
The Space Show
has already arrived.

01:31:07.040 --> 01:31:10.460
I'm guessing they're
setting up somewhere.

01:31:10.460 --> 01:31:13.130
That means we don't
have much time.

01:31:13.130 --> 01:31:14.970
We should split up
and search.

01:31:14.970 --> 01:31:17.510
Use the utmost caution.
Neppo is dangerous.

01:31:17.510 --> 01:31:18.930
- Roger!
- Roger!

01:31:18.930 --> 01:31:21.600
I wonder where the
Space Show is hiding.

01:31:21.600 --> 01:31:23.310
It should have started,
like, 20 minutes ago.

01:31:26.060 --> 01:31:27.560
Ladies and aliens...

01:31:27.560 --> 01:31:29.520
I love you, Neppo!

01:31:29.520 --> 01:31:33.280
Hurry! I want to see
the Space Show now!

01:31:35.150 --> 01:31:37.570
So, this is Zughaan?

01:31:37.570 --> 01:31:40.700
Well, you're in luck.
That's my very last one.

01:31:40.700 --> 01:31:42.330
How about I give you a deal?

01:31:42.330 --> 01:31:44.040
Just 10,000 pods for it.

01:31:44.040 --> 01:31:45.580
OK, sounds good.

01:31:45.580 --> 01:31:49.120
Please make the receipt
out to the Space Control Center.

01:31:49.120 --> 01:31:51.290
- He's a fraud!
- Huh?

01:31:51.290 --> 01:31:54.050
It's a fake. It's
completely synthetic.

01:31:54.050 --> 01:31:55.460
What do you want?

01:31:55.460 --> 01:31:57.800
Can't you see
that I'm busy?

01:31:57.800 --> 01:32:00.180
Let's make a deal.
Listen...

01:32:00.180 --> 01:32:03.680
I know who the leader of the
Zughann black market ring is.

01:32:18.190 --> 01:32:20.950
Sorry. Excuse me.

01:32:22.320 --> 01:32:23.620
Hey, Ink!

01:32:23.620 --> 01:32:25.620
Huh?

01:32:25.620 --> 01:32:28.080
Koji!

01:32:28.080 --> 01:32:30.620
Hello! Anyone there?

01:32:30.620 --> 01:32:33.630
Koji, can you hear me?

01:32:33.630 --> 01:32:36.210
Tony, were you able to
connect with the Center?

01:32:36.210 --> 01:32:39.590
Yes. It turns out your samples
are from the wasabi plant

01:32:39.590 --> 01:32:42.180
a different species
in the same family as Zughaan.

01:32:42.180 --> 01:32:44.260
You deserve the Executive
Director's award

01:32:44.260 --> 01:32:45.640
for this discovery.

01:32:45.640 --> 01:32:47.310
You can have my award.

01:32:47.310 --> 01:32:48.600
This is important.

01:32:48.600 --> 01:32:50.730
I need you to get the data
I requested.

01:32:52.520 --> 01:32:55.020
What about you guys?
Have you found anything?

01:32:55.020 --> 01:32:56.480
No.

01:32:56.480 --> 01:32:57.820
Sorry.

01:32:57.820 --> 01:32:59.490
We've searched everywhere.

01:32:59.490 --> 01:33:01.070
I've had no luck either.

01:33:01.070 --> 01:33:03.620
I'm sorry. I wasn't able
to help you.

01:33:03.620 --> 01:33:06.200
It's OK.

01:33:06.200 --> 01:33:08.620
Oh, hey!
The ship's finished.

01:33:08.620 --> 01:33:10.500
You should ask my dad
to give you a ride

01:33:10.500 --> 01:33:12.620
when he returns
from his meeting.

01:33:12.620 --> 01:33:16.250
Yeah. That'd be a lot of fun.

01:33:16.250 --> 01:33:17.630
- Huh?
- Huh?

01:33:17.630 --> 01:33:19.760
It's the supernova!

01:33:21.300 --> 01:33:22.760
Oh!

01:33:57.710 --> 01:33:59.800
Beautiful!

01:34:03.510 --> 01:34:07.430
I can't believe
I just saw a supernova.

01:34:12.850 --> 01:34:17.730
Happy Birthday to you

01:34:17.730 --> 01:34:19.150
Marie!

01:34:19.150 --> 01:34:23.570
Happy Birthday to you

01:34:23.570 --> 01:34:26.740
Happy Birthday--
- There they are!

01:34:26.740 --> 01:34:31.370
...supernova

01:34:31.370 --> 01:34:40.460
Happy Birthday to you

01:34:47.140 --> 01:34:49.300
Whoa! My goodness!

01:34:49.300 --> 01:34:50.760
So, that's what
they were hiding.

01:34:50.760 --> 01:34:52.850
So sneaky!

01:34:54.310 --> 01:34:56.310
- Let's meet back up.
- Where?

01:34:56.310 --> 01:34:57.850
At Goba's.

01:34:57.850 --> 01:35:01.320
Wait. I'm too far away.
It'll take too long.

01:35:01.320 --> 01:35:03.860
Koji's the closest.
We should meet there.

01:35:03.860 --> 01:35:05.400
Got it!

01:35:05.400 --> 01:35:07.360
Oh! Yay!

01:35:07.360 --> 01:35:10.370
Hello, ladies
and gentlealiens.

01:35:10.370 --> 01:35:12.200
Tonight is
a momentous occasion.

01:35:12.200 --> 01:35:13.500
Ohh...

01:35:13.500 --> 01:35:16.370
Yes. Believe it or not,
this is it--

01:35:16.370 --> 01:35:19.420
the very end
of the Space Show,

01:35:19.420 --> 01:35:21.380
but let there be no tears,

01:35:21.380 --> 01:35:26.300
because, fear not,
the Space Show will be reborn

01:35:26.300 --> 01:35:29.760
from the place marked
by this supernova!

01:35:29.760 --> 01:35:32.810
I present the space
Iron Mask at his best.

01:35:32.810 --> 01:35:34.890
Whoo-hoo!

01:35:42.650 --> 01:35:45.440
Princess Crystal
is being held hostage

01:35:45.440 --> 01:35:46.950
at the Black Castle.

01:35:46.950 --> 01:35:50.660
The Iron Mask slips in
all by himself to rescue her,

01:35:50.660 --> 01:35:52.620
but something is in the way.

01:35:52.620 --> 01:35:53.790
[Indistinct]

01:35:53.790 --> 01:35:55.330
It's the beast
of ancient lore...

01:35:55.330 --> 01:35:56.660
It's just Marie.

01:35:56.660 --> 01:35:58.000
The Behemoth!

01:36:06.970 --> 01:36:09.430
Is that the Behemoth?

01:36:09.430 --> 01:36:12.930
Will the Iron Mask successfully
defeat the Behemoth?

01:36:12.930 --> 01:36:15.430
Is that what they used
the Zughaan for?

01:36:15.430 --> 01:36:20.400
And finally, will we find out
the identity of the Iron Mask?

01:36:20.400 --> 01:36:23.440
But first, it's time for
a commercial break.

01:36:23.440 --> 01:36:26.150
A fateful time for
the universe is here.

01:36:26.150 --> 01:36:28.860
It's the biggest reform
since the Big Bang--

01:36:28.860 --> 01:36:30.860
I'm about to become a god.

01:36:30.860 --> 01:36:34.830
no one has ever seen,
will emerge from the ashes.

01:36:34.830 --> 01:36:37.580
The universe
has become reborn.

01:36:45.880 --> 01:36:48.550
We have to hurry up
and rescue her!

01:36:48.550 --> 01:36:50.880
How the heck are we
gonna get up there?

01:36:50.880 --> 01:36:52.970
Help us, Pochi!

01:36:58.890 --> 01:37:00.980
Ah! We have a rocket!

01:37:10.650 --> 01:37:12.530
- 3!
- 2!

01:37:12.530 --> 01:37:14.990
- 1!
- Go!

01:37:28.920 --> 01:37:31.630
Princess Crystal
is unable to sing.

01:37:31.630 --> 01:37:35.640
Only the bravest man in the
universe can save her now.

01:37:47.230 --> 01:37:50.490
Hang on, Amane!

01:37:56.620 --> 01:37:58.030
Oh!

01:38:00.410 --> 01:38:01.870
All right!

01:38:01.870 --> 01:38:04.330
We did it,
just in time.

01:38:05.920 --> 01:38:09.050
Talk about unexpected
guest stars.

01:38:11.920 --> 01:38:13.470
That's enough!

01:38:13.470 --> 01:38:18.050
I am sick of you
trying to get in my way.

01:38:29.980 --> 01:38:32.440
Ladies and aliens...

01:38:32.440 --> 01:38:36.950
Must have dozed off.
Could you fill me in?

01:38:36.950 --> 01:38:38.990
Did you see?
Natsuki really did it!

01:38:38.990 --> 01:38:40.580
Yeah.

01:38:43.410 --> 01:38:46.830
- Hey! We're here!
- Are you all right, Amane?

01:38:49.000 --> 01:38:50.920
Is that Natsuki?

01:38:50.920 --> 01:38:52.130
Pochi!

01:38:52.130 --> 01:38:54.380
We're gonna get you
out of there!

01:38:54.380 --> 01:38:57.590
Natsuki!
Pochi!

01:38:57.590 --> 01:38:59.100
We'll be right there!

01:39:02.350 --> 01:39:04.480
It's the end of the line.

01:39:06.980 --> 01:39:09.110
It's show time!

01:39:17.660 --> 01:39:19.910
We meet again, Pochi!

01:39:19.910 --> 01:39:22.040
It's been a while,
hasn't it?

01:39:22.040 --> 01:39:23.490
Neppo.

01:39:23.490 --> 01:39:26.000
What are you up to
this time?

01:39:26.000 --> 01:39:29.000
Eh, I'm just wondering...

01:39:29.000 --> 01:39:31.920
whether or not we should take
you with us to the new world.

01:39:31.920 --> 01:39:33.380
What are you talking about?

01:39:36.970 --> 01:39:40.140
I'm talking about
the Pet Star.

01:39:41.890 --> 01:39:44.020
I was the one
who found it.

01:39:44.020 --> 01:39:45.810
Aren't you proud of me?

01:40:13.880 --> 01:40:16.130
Huh? It's the Pet Star.

01:40:16.130 --> 01:40:19.510
The Space Show
is the Pet Star?

01:40:19.510 --> 01:40:21.640
Amazing!

01:40:21.640 --> 01:40:24.010
So it really does exist.

01:40:28.060 --> 01:40:32.110
Welcome, everyone.
This is the Pet Star.

01:40:32.110 --> 01:40:35.730
The world is one big family.

01:40:35.730 --> 01:40:37.530
We are all alien brethren.

01:40:37.530 --> 01:40:43.120
Ladies and gentlealiens,
I am Pet Star.

01:40:43.120 --> 01:40:45.080
I learned everything--

01:40:45.080 --> 01:40:48.500
- Inside. Take cover!
- Hurry! In here!

01:40:48.500 --> 01:40:51.040
- Look!
- Look.

01:40:51.040 --> 01:40:53.420
It's the same stuff
that kidnapped Amane!

01:40:53.420 --> 01:40:55.550
We are working hard
every day and every...

01:40:57.880 --> 01:41:00.720
Hey, guys, you all right?

01:41:00.720 --> 01:41:04.760
The whole universe
is one big family!

01:41:04.760 --> 01:41:07.100
We are all alien brethren.

01:41:07.100 --> 01:41:10.100
Everyone,
we are the Pet Star!

01:41:10.100 --> 01:41:12.520
So, the kidnapping
was intentional.

01:41:12.520 --> 01:41:17.020
It was the will
of the Pet Star.

01:41:26.280 --> 01:41:30.080
You're not even questioning
whether it's the real thing.

01:41:30.080 --> 01:41:32.170
I didn't once I saw
the Behemoth.

01:41:32.170 --> 01:41:37.090
Where do you think
I found it?

01:41:37.090 --> 01:41:40.630
Disappointed you
didn't find it?

01:41:40.630 --> 01:41:42.260
Hmm?

01:41:45.800 --> 01:41:48.890
It was in
the Dark Triangle.

01:42:07.450 --> 01:42:10.200
It had been asleep
for 5 billion years

01:42:10.200 --> 01:42:11.830
in the Sea of Antimatter.

01:42:11.830 --> 01:42:14.790
It was only in the midst
of the darkest despair

01:42:14.790 --> 01:42:16.580
that we finally arrived
at the truth.

01:42:16.580 --> 01:42:18.840
Marie!

01:42:18.840 --> 01:42:22.010
I think it's about time
that you left the stage,

01:42:22.010 --> 01:42:23.380
don't you?

01:42:23.380 --> 01:42:24.720
Not without Amane!

01:42:24.720 --> 01:42:27.890
This girl's so important,
is she now?

01:42:30.180 --> 01:42:32.020
Don't touch her!

01:42:34.890 --> 01:42:36.190
Amane!

01:42:36.190 --> 01:42:37.900
They're getting away!

01:42:37.900 --> 01:42:40.320
- Natsuki!
- We're coming!

01:42:41.780 --> 01:42:44.950
Pochi, help me!

01:42:47.530 --> 01:42:48.950
No!

01:42:50.450 --> 01:42:53.250
You and I are going
to settle this.

01:43:13.470 --> 01:43:16.640
- Natsuki, I'm here!
- Give it up, you.

01:43:16.640 --> 01:43:18.270
Let Amane go!

01:43:18.270 --> 01:43:20.360
You let go.

01:43:28.280 --> 01:43:29.990
That was easy.

01:43:54.220 --> 01:43:55.930
I'm not dead!

01:43:55.930 --> 01:43:57.230
Natsuki, are you all right?

01:43:57.230 --> 01:43:59.310
- Kiyoshi!
- I'm glad I reached you.

01:43:59.310 --> 01:44:01.900
Natsuki, are you OK?

01:44:01.900 --> 01:44:03.940
Yeah, I'm fine, but
I don't know what to do.

01:44:03.940 --> 01:44:05.230
They still have Amane.

01:44:05.230 --> 01:44:07.820
We'll meet you
and save her together.

01:44:07.820 --> 01:44:09.110
OK.

01:44:09.110 --> 01:44:11.070
Goba, can you take us
to Natsuki?

01:44:11.070 --> 01:44:13.030
Natsuki, find me
your nearest landmark.

01:44:13.030 --> 01:44:14.410
Got it.

01:44:16.290 --> 01:44:17.870
What do you want
with Amane?

01:44:17.870 --> 01:44:20.420
She's going to become
Perfect Life Form Number 2.

01:44:21.880 --> 01:44:24.880
Perfect Life Forms
don't exist!

01:44:24.880 --> 01:44:27.420
That's where you're wrong.

01:44:29.010 --> 01:44:32.430
I'll do it with the power of
Zughaan and the Great King Pet.

01:44:34.810 --> 01:44:37.520
Great King Pet?
Tony!

01:44:37.520 --> 01:44:39.440
Great King Pet.

01:44:48.110 --> 01:44:49.360
Found it.

01:44:49.360 --> 01:44:50.950
The Great King Pet.

01:44:50.950 --> 01:44:54.280
He is the true ruler
of the planet.

01:44:54.280 --> 01:44:56.290
Where is he?

01:44:56.290 --> 01:45:00.460
A Central Tower. It's the
tallest building on the planet.

01:45:02.380 --> 01:45:04.290
Pet Star is a rescue craft

01:45:04.290 --> 01:45:06.960
that dates back hundreds of
millions of generations.

01:45:06.960 --> 01:45:09.470
It sheltered animals
that were near extinction,

01:45:09.470 --> 01:45:12.260
but one day, it vanished
without a trace,

01:45:12.260 --> 01:45:14.970
and it's been a space
legend ever since.

01:45:14.970 --> 01:45:17.010
That is, until
Neppo found it

01:45:17.010 --> 01:45:20.480
and the Show
opened its curtain.

01:45:58.930 --> 01:46:00.390
Surrender.

01:46:00.390 --> 01:46:01.930
You have no chance
of winning.

01:46:01.930 --> 01:46:04.230
That's your opinion.

01:46:26.040 --> 01:46:27.540
He's weakened now.

01:46:30.460 --> 01:46:33.090
Finish off the pesky kids!

01:46:33.090 --> 01:46:34.510
- Roger!
- Roger!

01:46:36.550 --> 01:46:37.850
Hey!

01:46:37.850 --> 01:46:40.260
- Natsuki!
- Natsuki!

01:46:40.260 --> 01:46:42.100
When we get
close enough, jump on!

01:46:42.100 --> 01:46:43.560
Got it!

01:46:46.100 --> 01:46:48.560
- You can do it!
- Hurry! Jump!

01:46:57.870 --> 01:46:59.200
Kiyoshi!

01:46:59.200 --> 01:47:01.080
Natsuki, are you OK?

01:47:01.080 --> 01:47:02.580
Yeah, we're good.

01:47:04.250 --> 01:47:07.210
Sorry! Can't stay!

01:47:10.210 --> 01:47:12.250
All right.

01:47:12.250 --> 01:47:14.090
Let's go.

01:47:14.090 --> 01:47:16.590
We're gonna rescue Amane!

01:47:21.600 --> 01:47:23.430
Don't worry.
You'll be fine.

01:47:23.430 --> 01:47:26.100
Remember, you're with
a superhero after all.

01:47:26.100 --> 01:47:29.520
Natsuki, I'll guide
you to the Tower.

01:47:29.520 --> 01:47:31.230
Thanks!

01:47:38.160 --> 01:47:39.410
This is bad, Ink.

01:47:39.410 --> 01:47:41.530
Don't worry.
We'll get away.

01:47:57.470 --> 01:48:00.180
What? Did he
kidnap them, too?

01:48:00.180 --> 01:48:01.680
What is this place?

01:48:03.100 --> 01:48:06.850
Doesn't this look like
a fun place to work?

01:48:06.850 --> 01:48:09.190
More like slave labor.

01:48:09.190 --> 01:48:11.520
One's supposed to earn
their own keep.

01:48:11.520 --> 01:48:14.570
Didn't they teach you that
in school?

01:48:14.570 --> 01:48:16.610
Enough!

01:48:18.150 --> 01:48:19.910
Is this the right way, Goba?

01:48:19.910 --> 01:48:22.200
You're doing great, Natsuki.

01:48:22.200 --> 01:48:23.660
Head for the jungle ahead.

01:48:32.380 --> 01:48:37.590
O Great King Pet,
I have brought you a sacrifice.

01:48:37.590 --> 01:48:39.680
Ohhh...

01:48:52.610 --> 01:48:55.520
Well...what have we here?

01:48:55.520 --> 01:48:58.190
She's adorable,
fantastic,

01:48:58.190 --> 01:49:00.400
but why is there
only 1?

01:49:00.400 --> 01:49:03.570
I cannot synthesize
with just 1.

01:49:03.570 --> 01:49:05.080
There's more.

01:49:08.410 --> 01:49:10.460
Pyon-Kichi!

01:49:24.140 --> 01:49:25.550
This is bad!

01:49:25.550 --> 01:49:28.560
Ink, can't we do something
to fight back?

01:49:28.560 --> 01:49:30.270
I'm working on it!

01:49:33.270 --> 01:49:34.560
Is he all right?

01:49:34.560 --> 01:49:37.730
Of course! He's
a Perfect Life Form!

01:49:39.190 --> 01:49:42.490
There's no future
in synthesized life forms!

01:49:42.490 --> 01:49:46.660
The future lies in creating
stronger life forms.

01:49:49.870 --> 01:49:51.620
You're wrong!

01:49:51.620 --> 01:49:54.580
The real future lies in
being self-sustainable!

01:49:54.580 --> 01:49:56.750
What you're doing
is playing God!

01:50:05.140 --> 01:50:09.180
It's evil not to use your power
when you can save a world!

01:50:09.180 --> 01:50:11.980
Then why did this planet fall
in the first place?

01:50:21.360 --> 01:50:22.650
OK, which one?

01:50:22.650 --> 01:50:25.410
The blue one is
the water machine!

01:50:36.080 --> 01:50:37.790
Shoot it!

01:50:41.710 --> 01:50:43.800
Cool and refreshing!

01:50:46.800 --> 01:50:48.680
The water isn't working.

01:50:48.680 --> 01:50:50.600
We don't have anything else!

01:50:50.600 --> 01:50:52.140
Just keep shooting it!

01:51:13.700 --> 01:51:15.660
Its body temperature
is decreasing.

01:51:15.660 --> 01:51:17.830
He'll just have to
breathe more fire.

01:51:22.090 --> 01:51:23.760
Why isn't it coming out?

01:51:23.760 --> 01:51:25.550
It's working.

01:51:26.760 --> 01:51:29.390
Ink, fly alongside it!

01:51:29.390 --> 01:51:31.260
Leave it to me!

01:52:18.480 --> 01:52:19.900
Behemoth.

01:52:41.250 --> 01:52:43.380
Why?

01:52:43.380 --> 01:52:47.710
It's the difference between
Zughaan and wasabi.

01:52:47.710 --> 01:52:49.420
I feel bad for it,

01:52:49.420 --> 01:52:51.930
but the poor thing
was never meant to be.

01:52:54.470 --> 01:52:56.470
I did the test,

01:52:56.470 --> 01:52:59.850
and the margin of error
was within an acceptable range.

01:52:59.850 --> 01:53:01.850
Admit your mistakes.

01:53:03.060 --> 01:53:04.730
We're not God,

01:53:04.730 --> 01:53:07.730
and we don't have the right
to play with others' lives.

01:53:08.860 --> 01:53:11.660
There you go again.

01:53:11.660 --> 01:53:13.450
It doesn't matter
what I do.

01:53:13.450 --> 01:53:16.540
You always have to
contradict me!

01:53:16.540 --> 01:53:17.870
I've had it!

01:53:17.870 --> 01:53:20.580
Stop getting in my way!

01:53:22.880 --> 01:53:24.460
Not gonna happen.

01:53:24.460 --> 01:53:26.590
As long as you
continue on this path,

01:53:26.590 --> 01:53:29.130
I will follow you wherever
you go and stop you.

01:53:30.470 --> 01:53:32.800
You've changed, Neppo.

01:53:32.800 --> 01:53:34.970
Stop this before
it's too late.

01:53:39.350 --> 01:53:41.730
I know there is good in you.
- That's enough!

01:53:41.730 --> 01:53:43.600
Shut up!

01:54:21.520 --> 01:54:26.100
I wish we could go back
to the way things were.

01:54:26.100 --> 01:54:28.230
The 3 of us
were so happy.

01:54:31.900 --> 01:54:34.950
You know, I always
looked up to you, Neppo.

01:54:34.950 --> 01:54:37.200
You were my friend.

01:54:47.960 --> 01:54:51.050
Pochi!

01:55:03.520 --> 01:55:06.100
Kiyoshi.
I'm done over here.

01:55:07.520 --> 01:55:10.020
OK. I'll come
meet you.

01:55:19.240 --> 01:55:20.910
Don't be scared.

01:55:20.910 --> 01:55:23.000
They'll come
rescue us soon.

01:55:23.000 --> 01:55:25.410
Who will? Pochi?

01:55:27.500 --> 01:55:29.080
It's done!

01:55:31.630 --> 01:55:32.840
Look!

01:55:32.840 --> 01:55:35.590
See how cool
and cute you'll be?

01:55:35.590 --> 01:55:37.090
Isn't it hip?

01:55:39.890 --> 01:55:43.060
Stop it! No!

01:55:47.100 --> 01:55:48.730
Help me!

01:56:06.120 --> 01:56:09.120
Hey! Let me out!

01:56:17.760 --> 01:56:19.130
Natsuki!

01:56:22.760 --> 01:56:25.770
Amane!

01:56:35.690 --> 01:56:37.150
Take that!

01:56:38.860 --> 01:56:40.860
You brat!

01:56:40.860 --> 01:56:42.240
Oh!

01:56:47.700 --> 01:56:49.710
You came, Natsuki!

01:56:49.710 --> 01:56:51.170
Amane!

01:56:55.090 --> 01:56:56.590
Whaa...

01:56:58.550 --> 01:57:00.090
I'm gonna get you
out of there.

01:57:00.090 --> 01:57:01.800
OK.

01:57:13.730 --> 01:57:15.400
Who are you?

01:57:15.400 --> 01:57:19.190
People call me
the Summer Sister!

01:57:20.700 --> 01:57:22.070
I'm Natsuki Koyama.

01:57:22.070 --> 01:57:23.740
I've never heard of you.

01:57:23.740 --> 01:57:25.740
I don't care who you are.

01:57:25.740 --> 01:57:27.830
Just don't get in my way!

01:57:33.080 --> 01:57:35.040
That's my line!

01:57:35.040 --> 01:57:38.130
I'm sick of you guys
ruining my summer vacation!

01:57:38.130 --> 01:57:41.130
You better let Amane go!

01:57:41.130 --> 01:57:43.050
Not a chance!

01:57:43.050 --> 01:57:47.060
After all, she can't survive
in space unless I modify her.

01:57:47.060 --> 01:57:51.230
Look at her. She's still
too small and weak.

01:57:53.060 --> 01:57:55.150
That's where you're wrong.

01:57:55.150 --> 01:57:58.650
Amane is strong!

01:57:58.650 --> 01:58:01.070
She's mature,
and she's smart.

01:58:01.070 --> 01:58:04.160
I'm sure that...
did at first.

01:58:04.160 --> 01:58:05.530
Huh?

01:58:05.530 --> 01:58:08.120
I wanted her to rely on me
like she did before.

01:58:08.120 --> 01:58:10.700
It made me sad that
she acted like that

01:58:10.700 --> 01:58:13.370
because I thought she
didn't need me any more!

01:58:13.370 --> 01:58:15.750
I always knew that
Amane was strong,

01:58:15.750 --> 01:58:17.750
but I wanted her to be weak,

01:58:17.750 --> 01:58:19.750
because the truth is
I was weak

01:58:19.750 --> 01:58:22.510
and I needed that
in order to feel strong.

01:58:23.880 --> 01:58:28.260
That way, I could always
be her hero.

01:58:31.140 --> 01:58:33.270
It was totally wrong of me.

01:58:34.810 --> 01:58:36.150
And I know that now.

01:58:36.150 --> 01:58:37.650
I don't know what
you're talking about.

01:58:37.650 --> 01:58:42.070
I understand. It's OK.
I understand, Natsuki.

01:58:43.820 --> 01:58:45.910
Thank you.

01:58:49.830 --> 01:58:51.290
No!

01:58:54.210 --> 01:58:55.920
No!

01:58:58.170 --> 01:59:00.550
Out of the way.

01:59:00.550 --> 01:59:03.050
This time, I won't miss.

01:59:04.220 --> 01:59:05.970
Hurry up and do it!

01:59:07.800 --> 01:59:10.310
Don't!

01:59:15.190 --> 01:59:18.310
Oh! No! Help me!

01:59:22.940 --> 01:59:27.200
I'm also strong!

01:59:27.200 --> 01:59:29.620
Ah! Noriko!

01:59:29.620 --> 01:59:32.330
Way to go, Noriko!

02:00:04.400 --> 02:00:07.320
- Yay!
- Hooray!

02:00:07.320 --> 02:00:09.410
- That's it, girls.
Way to go.

02:00:09.410 --> 02:00:11.200
Whoo hoo hoo!

02:00:49.320 --> 02:00:51.200
I'm sorry.

02:00:51.200 --> 02:00:53.280
I'm sorry that we
didn't come sooner

02:00:53.280 --> 02:00:56.040
and that you had to
go through that alone.

02:01:00.250 --> 02:01:03.960
And I'm sorry that
I lost Pyon-Kichi.

02:01:03.960 --> 02:01:05.420
Hmm?

02:01:07.130 --> 02:01:10.260
I'll forgive you.

02:01:10.260 --> 02:01:14.430
Because you know what,
you're my hero, Natsuki.

02:01:20.350 --> 02:01:22.310
Your hair.

02:01:22.310 --> 02:01:24.940
Here, you want me
to fix it for you?

02:01:24.940 --> 02:01:27.440
Uh-huh.
Yes, please.

02:01:36.370 --> 02:01:39.450
Pyon-Kichi?

02:01:43.420 --> 02:01:44.960
It is Pyon-Kichi!

02:01:47.340 --> 02:01:50.090
- Pyon-Kichi!
- What are you doing here?

02:01:51.340 --> 02:01:54.720
Lucky you!
We can all go home now.

02:02:09.230 --> 02:02:11.950
- Hey!
- Hello!

02:02:11.950 --> 02:02:14.160
Over here!

02:02:14.160 --> 02:02:15.370
Hey!

02:02:15.370 --> 02:02:18.410
Boy, are we glad
to see you!

02:02:18.410 --> 02:02:20.040
Whoo hoo!

02:02:20.040 --> 02:02:21.500
Way to go!

02:02:24.000 --> 02:02:25.500
Well done!

02:02:28.420 --> 02:02:30.050
Whoo hoo!

02:02:30.050 --> 02:02:31.420
Way to go!

02:02:31.420 --> 02:02:33.050
Wow!

02:02:33.050 --> 02:02:34.380
Whoo hoo!

02:02:34.380 --> 02:02:37.140
- Yeah!
- This is amazing.

02:02:38.850 --> 02:02:40.520
Hey there!

02:02:41.810 --> 02:02:44.060
It's like being famous!

02:02:44.060 --> 02:02:45.850
Yeah!

02:02:45.850 --> 02:02:47.400
Look at that.

02:02:47.400 --> 02:02:49.980
It seems some new
stars were born.

02:02:49.980 --> 02:02:52.530
I'll log it
in the records.

02:02:55.110 --> 02:02:57.740
Oh! The police
have finally arrived.

02:02:57.740 --> 02:03:01.540
What's gonna happen
to Neppo?

02:03:01.540 --> 02:03:03.500
Well, he did commit
a crime,

02:03:03.500 --> 02:03:06.370
which means he'll probably
be punished accordingly.

02:03:09.380 --> 02:03:12.880
Now, then, why don't we
go back to Earth, huh?

02:03:12.880 --> 02:03:15.430
Yeah, it's about time.

02:03:15.430 --> 02:03:17.340
- Yeah.
- I miss home.

02:03:17.340 --> 02:03:19.390
We're gonna be getting
back a little late,

02:03:19.390 --> 02:03:21.430
but at least we'll
all get in trouble together.

02:03:21.430 --> 02:03:23.390
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

02:03:23.390 --> 02:03:25.350
- We'll make it.
- Huh?

02:03:25.350 --> 02:03:28.440
But there's only half an hour
before our parents get there.

02:03:28.440 --> 02:03:30.440
Don't worry. Trust me.

02:03:30.440 --> 02:03:32.440
We just have to
all work together.

02:03:32.440 --> 02:03:34.150
- Huh?
- What do you say?

02:03:34.150 --> 02:03:35.450
You want to give up?

02:03:35.450 --> 02:03:37.740
- Um-mmm.
- Um-mmm.

02:03:37.740 --> 02:03:39.410
Please clear the orbit.

02:03:39.410 --> 02:03:42.120
A group from Murakawa
Village Grade School

02:03:42.120 --> 02:03:43.540
will be passing through.

02:03:43.540 --> 02:03:46.540
We are making a stop
at the star.

02:03:46.540 --> 02:03:48.920
You should have seen it.
It was the coolest.

02:03:48.920 --> 02:03:51.960
That's right. Just opened up
the superspeed space.

02:04:06.640 --> 02:04:09.020
Thanks. Yes, that's
a big help, Duke.

02:04:09.020 --> 02:04:12.440
- Goba! Tony!
- Goba! Tony!

02:04:12.440 --> 02:04:15.490
- Thanks for everything!
- Thank you!

02:04:15.490 --> 02:04:19.360
- You were a great help!
- Bye! It was my pleasure.

02:04:19.360 --> 02:04:21.200
You kids were
a lot of fun.

02:04:21.200 --> 02:04:23.540
- Take care of yourselves!
- Take care of yourselves!

02:04:23.540 --> 02:04:25.500
Seriously, thank you!

02:04:25.500 --> 02:04:28.670
- You, too!
- Have a safe trip!

02:04:28.670 --> 02:04:30.630
We owe you big-time!

02:04:35.130 --> 02:04:38.130
Oh, hey, I am now
out of a job.

02:04:38.130 --> 02:04:40.090
You could come work with me
at the Space Center.

02:04:40.090 --> 02:04:43.560
- We're always short on staff.
- Are you serious?

02:04:43.560 --> 02:04:45.430
Thank you, Ink.

02:04:45.430 --> 02:04:47.310
No, thank you.

02:04:47.310 --> 02:04:50.270
It was great publicity
for my dad.

02:05:03.580 --> 02:05:05.620
See you later.

02:05:07.080 --> 02:05:09.210
Yeah.

02:05:09.210 --> 02:05:11.290
See you later.

02:05:18.510 --> 02:05:21.550
Bye, guys!
Have a safe trip!

02:05:21.550 --> 02:05:23.680
- See you later!
- Good-bye!

02:05:28.100 --> 02:05:31.190
- Amane?
- Hmm?

02:05:31.190 --> 02:05:34.190
I have sort of a silly
question to ask you.

02:05:34.190 --> 02:05:36.770
After I've sorted
stuff out here,

02:05:36.770 --> 02:05:39.860
that is, only if you
don't mind, of course,

02:05:39.860 --> 02:05:41.360
may I come and visit you?

02:05:41.360 --> 02:05:42.700
Huh?

02:05:44.200 --> 02:05:46.910
Can you?
Are you allowed?

02:05:46.910 --> 02:05:48.830
I can come in secret.

02:05:50.200 --> 02:05:51.910
I'll wait for you!

02:06:00.340 --> 02:06:01.720
Amane, I, uh...

02:06:03.590 --> 02:06:06.600
Pochi! What were you
doing to Amane?

02:06:06.600 --> 02:06:08.260
I didn't do anything!

02:06:08.260 --> 02:06:10.640
Then why are you blushing?

02:06:12.270 --> 02:06:14.940
Well, you're blushing, too!

02:06:14.940 --> 02:06:17.320
I'm innocent, I tell you!

02:06:23.660 --> 02:06:26.370
Thanks a lot, Pochi.

02:06:27.780 --> 02:06:29.660
Pochi.

02:06:29.660 --> 02:06:31.620
Pochi!

02:06:31.620 --> 02:06:34.370
- Pochi.
- Pochi.

02:06:40.300 --> 02:06:41.590
Oh, come on, stop.

02:06:41.590 --> 02:06:44.680
Stop it!
It's making me...

02:06:44.680 --> 02:06:47.390
No! Pochi!

02:06:50.640 --> 02:06:53.770
Natsuki, stop
touching my butt!

02:07:13.660 --> 02:07:15.580
We left them
completely alone.

02:07:15.580 --> 02:07:17.250
I hope they're OK.

02:07:17.250 --> 02:07:19.290
They should be fine.
Kiyoshi's with them.

02:07:19.290 --> 02:07:21.630
Noriko tends to get mad
if we check up on her too much.

02:07:21.630 --> 02:07:25.680
Oh, I never imagined
she'd be that way.

02:07:25.680 --> 02:07:29.800
Noriko is a pervert,
pervert, pervert!

02:07:32.140 --> 02:07:33.810
Oh!

02:07:42.360 --> 02:07:43.740
Huh?

02:07:43.740 --> 02:07:45.360
What are you kids doing?

02:07:45.360 --> 02:07:46.780
Why are you
by the window?

02:07:48.240 --> 02:07:49.820
Nothing.

02:07:52.540 --> 02:07:54.830
- Did something happen?
- Huh?

02:07:57.370 --> 02:07:59.130
Nope. Nothing.

02:08:00.290 --> 02:08:04.130
It was...it was fun,
wasn't it?

02:08:04.130 --> 02:08:06.170
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

02:08:17.390 --> 02:08:19.770
Hey, sis, look!

02:08:19.770 --> 02:08:21.310
Wow!

02:08:21.310 --> 02:08:23.230
Oh, that's
just a UFO.

02:08:32.370 --> 02:08:33.740
- Hey, Dad.
- Hmm?

02:08:33.740 --> 02:08:36.750
Do you have books
about astronauts at home?

02:08:36.750 --> 02:08:40.420
You know what, I believe
I do have one in the shed.

02:08:40.420 --> 02:08:42.000
Can I borrow it?

02:08:42.000 --> 02:08:44.380
- Mom?
- Mm-hmm?

02:08:44.380 --> 02:08:47.880
I think...I think
I want to become a doctor.

02:08:51.800 --> 02:08:53.890
I always thought you would.

02:09:51.860 --> 02:09:53.950
What a beautiful day!

02:10:01.790 --> 02:10:03.540
We're going to
the schoolhouse!

02:10:03.540 --> 02:10:05.330
Really? What for?

02:10:05.330 --> 02:10:07.750
We're gonna have a reunion!

02:10:07.750 --> 02:10:11.050
They've gotten so close.
It's nice.

02:10:11.050 --> 02:10:13.970
- Here we go!
- Go!

02:10:17.350 --> 02:10:20.980
- I'm gonna go fast!
- Whoo hoo!
